{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba experiments/zkir-k/semantics/zkir-values.k; nl -ba experiments/zkir-k/semantics/zkir-field.k'","aggregated_output":"     1\t// ZKIR v3 runtime values (ir_types.rs `IrValue`) and their encoding as raw\n     2\t// native field elements (ir_instructions/encode.rs, midnight-circuits 7.2.4\n     3\t// `Instantiable::as_public_input` / `from_public_input`).\n     4\t//\n     5\t//   Native            [x]\n     6\t//   Bytes32           [int_le(bytes[0..31]), bytes[31]]\n     7\t//   JubjubPoint       [x, y]  (affine twisted-Edwards coordinates)\n     8\t//   JubjubScalar      [s]     (252-bit scalar, one element)\n     9\t//   Foreign field K   limbs of (x - 1 mod p) in base 2^LOG2_BASE, NB_LIMBS limbs,\n    10\t//                     grouped 254/LOG2_BASE limbs per element:\n    11\t//                       secp256k1/secp256r1 base and scalar, Curve25519 base:\n    12\t//                         LOG2_BASE 64, 4 limbs, 3 per element  -> 2 elements\n    13\t//                       Curve25519 scalar: LOG2_BASE 51, 5 limbs, 4 per element -> 2 elements\n    14\t//   Weierstrass point enc(x) ++ enc(y) ++ [is_identity]; identity encodes (0,0),\n    15\t//                     i.e. enc(p-1) twice, then 1\n    16\t//   Curve25519 point  enc(x) ++ enc(y)\n    17\trequires \"zkir-syntax.k\"\n    18\trequires \"zkir-curves.k\"\n    19\t\n    20\tmodule ZKIR-VALUES\n    21\t  imports ZKIR-SYNTAX\n    22\t  imports ZKIR-CURVES\n    23\t  imports BYTES\n    24\t  imports LIST\n    25\t  imports STRING\n    26\t\n    27\t  syntax Value ::= native(Int)            [symbol(nativeV)]\n    28\t                 | bytes32(Bytes)         [symbol(bytes32V)]\n    29\t                 | jubjubPoint(Point)     [symbol(jubjubPointV)]\n    30\t                 | jubjubScalar(Int)      [symbol(jubjubScalarV)]\n    31\t                 | secp256k1Point(Point)  [symbol(secp256k1PointV)]\n    32\t                 | secp256k1Base(Int)     [symbol(secp256k1BaseV)]\n    33\t                 | secp256k1Scalar(Int)   [symbol(secp256k1ScalarV)]\n    34\t                 | secp256r1Point(Point)  [symbol(secp256r1PointV)]\n    35\t                 | secp256r1Base(Int)     [symbol(secp256r1BaseV)]\n    36\t                 | secp256r1Scalar(Int)   [symbol(secp256r1ScalarV)]\n    37\t                 | curve25519Point(Point) [symbol(curve25519PointV)]\n    38\t                 | curve25519Base(Int)    [symbol(curve25519BaseV)]\n    39\t                 | curve25519Scalar(Int)  [symbol(curve25519ScalarV)]\n    40\t\n    41\t  syntax IrType ::= typeOf(Value) [function, total]\n    42\t  rule typeOf(native(_))          => native()\n    43\t  rule typeOf(bytes32(_))         => bytes32()\n    44\t  rule typeOf(jubjubPoint(_))     => jubjubPoint()\n    45\t  rule typeOf(jubjubScalar(_))    => jubjubScalar()\n    46\t  rule typeOf(secp256k1Point(_))  => secp256k1Point()\n    47\t  rule typeOf(secp256k1Base(_))   => secp256k1Base()\n    48\t  rule typeOf(secp256k1Scalar(_)) => secp256k1Scalar()\n    49\t  rule typeOf(secp256r1Point(_))  => secp256r1Point()\n    50\t  rule typeOf(secp256r1Base(_))   => secp256r1Base()\n    51\t  rule typeOf(secp256r1Scalar(_)) => secp256r1Scalar()\n    52\t  rule typeOf(curve25519Point(_)) => curve25519Point()\n    53\t  rule typeOf(curve25519Base(_))  => curve25519Base()\n    54\t  rule typeOf(curve25519Scalar(_))=> curve25519Scalar()\n    55\t\n    56\t  // `IrValue::default(t)`: zero / identity of each type.\n    57\t  syntax Value ::= defaultValue(IrType) [function, total]\n    58\t  rule defaultValue(native())          => native(0)\n    59\t  rule defaultValue(bytes32())         => bytes32(padRightBytes(.Bytes, 32, 0))\n    60\t  rule defaultValue(jubjubPoint())     => jubjubPoint(pt(0, 1))\n    61\t  rule defaultValue(jubjubScalar())    => jubjubScalar(0)\n    62\t  rule defaultValue(secp256k1Point())  => secp256k1Point(inf())\n    63\t  rule defaultValue(secp256k1Base())   => secp256k1Base(0)\n    64\t  rule defaultValue(secp256k1Scalar()) => secp256k1Scalar(0)\n    65\t  rule defaultValue(secp256r1Point())  => secp256r1Point(inf())\n    66\t  rule defaultValue(secp256r1Base())   => secp256r1Base(0)\n    67\t  rule defaultValue(secp256r1Scalar()) => secp256r1Scalar(0)\n    68\t  rule defaultValue(curve25519Point()) => curve25519Point(pt(0, 1))\n    69\t  rule defaultValue(curve25519Base())  => curve25519Base(0)\n    70\t  rule defaultValue(curve25519Scalar())=> curve25519Scalar(0)\n    71\t\n    72\t  // Debug-style names matching the Rust variant names (used by the oracle).\n    73\t  syntax String ::= typeName(IrType) [function, total]\n    74\t  rule typeName(native())          => \"Native\"\n    75\t  rule typeName(bytes32())         => \"Bytes32\"\n    76\t  rule typeName(jubjubPoint())     => \"JubjubPoint\"\n    77\t  rule typeName(jubjubScalar())    => \"JubjubScalar\"\n    78\t  rule typeName(secp256k1Point())  => \"Secp256k1Point\"\n    79\t  rule typeName(secp256k1Base())   => \"Secp256k1Base\"\n    80\t  rule typeName(secp256k1Scalar()) => \"Secp256k1Scalar\"\n    81\t  rule typeName(secp256r1Point())  => \"Secp256r1Point\"\n    82\t  rule typeName(secp256r1Base())   => \"Secp256r1Base\"\n    83\t  rule typeName(secp256r1Scalar()) => \"Secp256r1Scalar\"\n    84\t  rule typeName(curve25519Point()) => \"Curve25519Point\"\n    85\t  rule typeName(curve25519Base())  => \"Curve25519Base\"\n    86\t  rule typeName(curve25519Scalar())=> \"Curve25519Scalar\"\n    87\t\n    88\t  // --- Foreign-field limb encoding -------------------------------------------------\n    89\t  // encForeign(x, p, log2Base, nbLimbs): list of native elements.\n    90\t  syntax List ::= encForeign(Int, Int, Int, Int) [function, total]\n    91\t  rule encForeign(X, P, L, NB) => #groupLimbs(fsub(X, 1, P), L, NB, 254 /Int L)\n    92\t  // #groupLimbs(e, log2Base, limbsLeft, perBatch): successive batches of perBatch limbs\n    93\t  syntax List ::= #groupLimbs(Int, Int, Int, Int) [function, total]\n    94\t  rule #groupLimbs(_, _, NB, _) => .List requires NB <=Int 0\n    95\t  rule #groupLimbs(E, L, NB, B) => ListItem(lowBits(E, L *Int minInt(NB, B))) #groupLimbs(highBits(E, L *Int minInt(NB, B)), L, NB -Int minInt(NB, B), B)\n    96\t    requires NB >Int 0\n    97\t\n    98\t  // decForeign(fields, p, log2Base, nbLimbs): the element, or -1 when the\n    99\t  // encoding is invalid (wrong count, batch too large, non-zero tail limbs).\n   100\t  syntax Int ::= decForeign(List, Int, Int, Int) [function, total]\n   101\t  rule decForeign(Fs, P, L, NB) => -1\n   102\t    requires size(Fs) =/=Int (NB +Int (254 /Int L) -Int 1) /Int (254 /Int L)\n   103\t  rule decForeign(Fs, P, L, NB) => #decForeign(Fs, P, L, NB, 254 /Int L, 0, 0)\n   104\t    requires size(Fs) ==Int (NB +Int (254 /Int L) -Int 1) /Int (254 /Int L)\n   105\t  // #decForeign(fields, p, log2, nb, perBatch, accumulated, limbsSeen)\n   106\t  syntax Int ::= #decForeign(List, Int, Int, Int, Int, Int, Int) [function, total]\n   107\t  rule #decForeign(.List, P, L, NB, _, Acc, _) => fadd(Acc, 1, P)\n   108\t    requires fitsBits(Acc, L *Int NB)\n   109\t  rule #decForeign(.List, _, L, NB, _, Acc, _) => -1\n   110\t    requires notBool fitsBits(Acc, L *Int NB)\n   111\t  rule #decForeign(ListItem(F) Fs, P, L, NB, B, Acc, Seen) => -1\n   112\t    requires notBool fitsBits(F, L *Int B)\n   113\t  rule #decForeign(ListItem(F) Fs, P, L, NB, B, Acc, Seen)\n   114\t    => #decForeign(Fs, P, L, NB, B, Acc +Int (F <<Int (L *Int Seen)), Seen +Int B)\n   115\t    requires fitsBits(F, L *Int B)\n   116\t\n   117\t  // Curve-specific parameters (LOG2_BASE, NB_LIMBS) over the BLS12-381 scalar field.\n   118\t  syntax List ::= encField64(Int, Int) [function, total]    // 64-bit limbs, 4 limbs\n   119\t  rule encField64(X, P) => encForeign(X, P, 64, 4)\n   120\t  syntax Int ::= decField64(List, Int) [function, total]\n   121\t  rule decField64(Fs, P) => decForeign(Fs, P, 64, 4)\n   122\t\n   123\t  // --- Points ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n   124\t  syntax List ::= encWPoint(Point, Int) [function, total]\n   125\t  rule encWPoint(inf(), P) => encField64(0, P) encField64(0, P) ListItem(1)\n   126\t  rule encWPoint(pt(X, Y), P) => encField64(X, P) encField64(Y, P) ListItem(0)\n   127\t  syntax List ::= encEPointForeign(Point, Int) [function, total]\n   128\t  rule encEPointForeign(pt(X, Y), P) => encField64(X, P) encField64(Y, P)\n   129\t  rule encEPointForeign(inf(), P) => encField64(0, P) encField64(1, P)\n   130\t\n   131\t  // --- Value encoding (encode_offcircuit) ---------------------------------------------\n   132\t  syntax List ::= encodeValue(Value) [function, total]\n   133\t  rule encodeValue(native(X))            => ListItem(X)\n   134\t  rule encodeValue(bytes32(B))           => ListItem(Bytes2Int(substrBytes(B, 0, 31), LE, Unsigned)) ListItem(B[31])\n   135\t  rule encodeValue(jubjubPoint(pt(X, Y))) => ListItem(X) ListItem(Y)\n   136\t  rule encodeValue(jubjubPoint(inf()))   => ListItem(0) ListItem(1)\n   137\t  rule encodeValue(jubjubScalar(S))      => ListItem(S)\n   138\t  rule encodeValue(secp256k1Point(Q))    => encWPoint(Q, #k256P)\n   139\t  rule encodeValue(secp256k1Base(X))     => encField64(X, #k256P)\n   140\t  rule encodeValue(secp256k1Scalar(X))   => encField64(X, #k256N)\n   141\t  rule encodeValue(secp256r1Point(Q))    => encWPoint(Q, #p256P)\n   142\t  rule encodeValue(secp256r1Base(X))     => encField64(X, #p256P)\n   143\t  rule encodeValue(secp256r1Scalar(X))   => encField64(X, #p256N)\n   144\t  rule encodeValue(curve25519Point(Q))   => encEPointForeign(Q, #c25519P)\n   145\t  rule encodeValue(curve25519Base(X))    => encField64(X, #c25519P)\n   146\t  rule encodeValue(curve25519Scalar(X))  => encForeign(X, #c25519L, 51, 5)\n   147\t\n   148\t  // --- Value decoding (decode_offcircuit) -------------------------------------------------\n   149\t  syntax DecodeResult ::= decOk(Value) | decErr(String)\n   150\t\n   151\t  syntax DecodeResult ::= decodeValue(List, IrType) [function, total]\n   152\t  rule decodeValue(ListItem(X), native()) => decOk(native(X))\n   153\t  rule decodeValue(Fs, native()) => decErr(\"Failed to decode as Native\") requires size(Fs) =/=Int 1\n   154\t\n   155\t  // Bytes32: the Rust decoder asserts (panics) when the low element uses byte\n   156\t  // 31 or the high element exceeds one byte; both are errors here.\n   157\t  rule decodeValue(ListItem(Lo) ListItem(Hi), bytes32())\n   158\t    => decOk(bytes32(replaceAtBytes(Int2Bytes(32, Lo, LE), 31, Int2Bytes(1, Hi, LE))))\n   159\t    requires fitsBits(Lo, 248) andBool fitsBits(Hi, 8)\n   160\t  rule decodeValue(ListItem(Lo) ListItem(Hi), bytes32()) => decErr(\"Bytes32 decoding assertion failed\")\n   161\t    requires notBool (fitsBits(Lo, 248) andBool fitsBits(Hi, 8))\n   162\t  rule decodeValue(Fs, bytes32()) => decErr(\"Failed to decode as Bytes32\") requires size(Fs) =/=Int 2\n   163\t\n   164\t  rule decodeValue(ListItem(X) ListItem(Y), jubjubPoint()) => #decJubjub(jubjubFromXY(X, Y))\n   165\t  rule decodeValue(Fs, jubjubPoint()) => decErr(\"Failed to decode as JubjubPoint\") requires size(Fs) =/=Int 2\n   166\t  syntax DecodeResult ::= #decJubjub(PointResult) [function, total]\n   167\t  rule #decJubjub(ptErr(_)) => decErr(\"Failed to decode as JubjubPoint\")\n   168\t  rule #decJubjub(ptOk(Q)) => decOk(jubjubPoint(Q)) requires inSubgroup(#jubjub, Q)\n   169\t  rule #decJubjub(ptOk(Q)) => decErr(\"Failed to decode as JubjubPoint\") requires notBool inSubgroup(#jubjub, Q)\n   170\t\n   171\t  // JubjubScalar: one element below 2^254; its low 252 bits must be a canonical\n   172\t  // scalar (AssignedScalarOfNativeCurve::from_public_input).\n   173\t  rule decodeValue(ListItem(F), jubjubScalar()) => decOk(jubjubScalar(lowBits(F, 252)))\n   174\t    requires fitsBits(F, 254) andBool lowBits(F, 252) <Int #rJ\n   175\t  rule decodeValue(ListItem(F), jubjubScalar()) => decErr(\"Failed to decode as JubjubScalar\")\n   176\t    requires notBool (fitsBits(F, 254) andBool lowBits(F, 252) <Int #rJ)\n   177\t  rule decodeValue(Fs, jubjubScalar()) => decErr(\"Failed to decode as JubjubScalar\") requires size(Fs) =/=Int 1\n   178\t\n   179\t  rule decodeValue(Fs, secp256k1Base())   => #decField(decField64(Fs, #k256P), secp256k1Base())\n   180\t  rule decodeValue(Fs, secp256k1Scalar()) => #decField(decField64(Fs, #k256N), secp256k1Scalar())\n   181\t  rule decodeValue(Fs, secp256r1Base())   => #decField(decField64(Fs, #p256P), secp256r1Base())\n   182\t  rule decodeValue(Fs, secp256r1Scalar()) => #decField(decField64(Fs, #p256N), secp256r1Scalar())\n   183\t  rule decodeValue(Fs, curve25519Base())  => #decField(decField64(Fs, #c25519P), curve25519Base())\n   184\t  rule decodeValue(Fs, curve25519Scalar())=> #decField(decForeign(Fs, #c25519L, 51, 5), curve25519Scalar())\n   185\t  syntax DecodeResult ::= #decField(Int, IrType) [function, total]\n   186\t  rule #decField(-1, T) => decErr(\"Failed to decode as \" +String typeName(T))\n   187\t  rule #decField(X, secp256k1Base())    => decOk(secp256k1Base(X))    requires X >=Int 0\n   188\t  rule #decField(X, secp256k1Scalar())  => decOk(secp256k1Scalar(X))  requires X >=Int 0\n   189\t  rule #decField(X, secp256r1Base())    => decOk(secp256r1Base(X))    requires X >=Int 0\n   190\t  rule #decField(X, secp256r1Scalar())  => decOk(secp256r1Scalar(X))  requires X >=Int 0\n   191\t  rule #decField(X, curve25519Base())   => decOk(curve25519Base(X))   requires X >=Int 0\n   192\t  rule #decField(X, curve25519Scalar()) => decOk(curve25519Scalar(X)) requires X >=Int 0\n   193\t  rule #decField(_, T) => decErr(\"Failed to decode as \" +String typeName(T)) [owise]\n   194\t\n   195\t  // Weierstrass points: 5 elements; last == 1 means identity.\n   196\t  rule decodeValue(Fs, secp256k1Point()) => #decWPoint(Fs, #secp256k1, secp256k1Point())\n   197\t  rule decodeValue(Fs, secp256r1Point()) => #decWPoint(Fs, #secp256r1, secp256r1Point())\n   198\t  syntax DecodeResult ::= #decWPoint(List, Curve, IrType) [function, total]\n   199\t  rule #decWPoint(Fs, C, T) => decErr(\"Failed to decode as \" +String typeName(T)) requires size(Fs) =/=Int 5\n   200\t  rule #decWPoint(Fs, C, T) => decOk(#wrapPoint(inf(), T)) requires size(Fs) ==Int 5 andBool Fs[4] ==K 1\n   201\t  rule #decWPoint(Fs, C, T) => #decWPointXY(decField64(range(Fs, 0, 3), curveField(C)), decField64(range(Fs, 2, 1), curveField(C)), C, T)\n   202\t    requires size(Fs) ==Int 5 andBool Fs[4] =/=K 1\n   203\t  syntax DecodeResult ::= #decWPointXY(Int, Int, Curve, IrType) [function, total]\n   204\t  rule #decWPointXY(X, Y, C, T) => decErr(\"Failed to decode as \" +String typeName(T)) requires X <Int 0 orBool Y <Int 0\n   205\t  rule #decWPointXY(X, Y, C, T) => #decPointResult(fromXY(C, X, Y), C, T) requires X >=Int 0 andBool Y >=Int 0\n   206\t  syntax DecodeResult ::= #decPointResult(PointResult, Curve, IrType) [function, total]\n   207\t  rule #decPointResult(ptErr(_), _, T) => decErr(\"Failed to decode as \" +String typeName(T))\n   208\t  rule #decPointResult(ptOk(Q), C, T) => decOk(#wrapPoint(Q, T)) requires inSubgroup(C, Q)\n   209\t  rule #decPointResult(ptOk(Q), C, T) => decErr(\"Failed to decode as \" +String typeName(T)) requires notBool inSubgroup(C, Q)\n   210\t\n   211\t  // Curve25519 points: 4 elements, exact curve check then subgroup check.\n   212\t  rule decodeValue(Fs, curve25519Point()) => decErr(\"Failed to decode as Curve25519Point\") requires size(Fs) =/=Int 4\n   213\t  rule decodeValue(Fs, curve25519Point())\n   214\t    => #decWPointXY(decField64(range(Fs, 0, 2), #c25519P), decField64(range(Fs, 2, 0), #c25519P), #curve25519, curve25519Point())\n   215\t    requires size(Fs) ==Int 4\n   216\t\n   217\t  syntax Value ::= #wrapPoint(Point, IrType) [function, total]\n   218\t  rule #wrapPoint(Q, secp256k1Point())  => secp256k1Point(Q)\n   219\t  rule #wrapPoint(Q, secp256r1Point())  => secp256r1Point(Q)\n   220\t  rule #wrapPoint(Q, curve25519Point()) => curve25519Point(Q)\n   221\t  rule #wrapPoint(Q, jubjubPoint())     => jubjubPoint(Q)\n   222\t  rule #wrapPoint(_, _)                 => native(0) [owise]\n   223\t\n   224\t  // Strict decoding re-encodes the value and demands the original elements\n   225\t  // (midnight-zkir 2ffe2d1 `decode_offcircuit`); 92e8bdd3 does not check.\n   226\t  syntax DecodeResult ::= decodeStrict(List, IrType, Bool) [function, total]\n   227\t  rule decodeStrict(L, T, false) => decodeValue(L, T)\n   228\t  rule decodeStrict(L, T, true) => #canonical(decodeValue(L, T), L, T)\n   229\t  syntax DecodeResult ::= #canonical(DecodeResult, List, IrType) [function, total]\n   230\t  rule #canonical(decErr(S), _, _) => decErr(S)\n   231\t  rule #canonical(decOk(V), L, _) => decOk(V) requires encodeValue(V) ==K L\n   232\t  rule #canonical(decOk(V), L, T) => decErr(\"The encoded value of type \" +String typeName(T) +String \" is not in canonical form\") requires encodeValue(V) =/=K L\n   233\t\n   234\t  // Decode a whole raw vector by a list of types (inputs of a program):\n   235\t  // decodeMany(raw, types) is decManyOk(values) or decErr; the Rust code\n   236\t  // reports running out of inputs and leftover inputs as separate errors.\n   237\t  syntax DecodeMany ::= decManyOk(List) | decManyErr(String)\n   238\t  syntax DecodeMany ::= decodeInputs(List, TypedIds, Int, Bool) [function, total]   // (raw, inputs, index, strict)\n   239\t  rule decodeInputs(Raw, .TypedIds, Idx, _) => decManyOk(.List) requires Idx ==Int size(Raw)\n   240\t  rule decodeInputs(Raw, .TypedIds, Idx, _) => decManyErr(\"Expected \" +String Int2String(Idx) +String \" raw inputs, received \" +String Int2String(size(Raw)))\n   241\t    requires Idx =/=Int size(Raw)\n   242\t  rule decodeInputs(Raw, (typedId(N, T), _), Idx, _)\n   243\t    => decManyErr(\"Not enough raw inputs: ran out at index \" +String Int2String(Idx) +String \" while decoding \" +String N)\n   244\t    requires Idx +Int encodedLen(T) >Int size(Raw)\n   245\t  rule decodeInputs(Raw, (typedId(N, T), Rest), Idx, Strict)\n   246\t    => #consDecoded(decodeStrict(range(Raw, Idx, size(Raw) -Int Idx -Int encodedLen(T)), T, Strict), N, decodeInputs(Raw, Rest, Idx +Int encodedLen(T), Strict))\n   247\t    requires Idx +Int encodedLen(T) <=Int size(Raw)\n   248\t  syntax DecodeMany ::= #consDecoded(DecodeResult, String, DecodeMany) [function, total]\n   249\t  rule #consDecoded(decErr(S), _, _) => decManyErr(S)\n   250\t  rule #consDecoded(decOk(_), _, decManyErr(S)) => decManyErr(S)\n   251\t  rule #consDecoded(decOk(V), N, decManyOk(L)) => decManyOk(ListItem(binding(N, V)) L)\n   252\t  syntax Binding ::= binding(String, Value)\n   253\t\n   254\t  // --- Bytes32 helpers ------------------------------------------------------------------\n   255\t  // Canonical little-endian 32-byte form of a field element (into_bytes32).\n   256\t  syntax Bytes ::= intToBytes32(Int) [function, total]\n   257\t  rule intToBytes32(X) => Int2Bytes(32, X, LE) requires X >=Int 0\n   258\t  rule intToBytes32(_) => padRightBytes(.Bytes, 32, 0) [owise]\n   259\t  syntax Int ::= bytes32ToInt(Bytes) [function, total]\n   260\t  rule bytes32ToInt(B) => Bytes2Int(B, LE, Unsigned)\n   261\tendmodule\n     1\t// Prime-field arithmetic over K's arbitrary-precision Int (plan decision\n     2\t// CLM-0709). Every function takes the modulus explicitly; results are kept in\n     3\t// canonical range [0, p) with modInt (Euclidean, never negative).\n     4\t//\n     5\t// Moduli (midnight-curves 0.3.1):\n     6\t//   r      BLS12-381 scalar field = ZKIR native field = Jubjub base field\n     7\t//   rJ     Jubjub scalar field (prime-order subgroup order)\n     8\t//   k256P  secp256k1 base field, k256N its group order\n     9\t//   p256P  secp256r1 base field, p256N its group order\n    10\t//   c25519P = 2^255 - 19, c25519L = 2^252 + 27742317777372353535851937790883648493\n    11\tmodule ZKIR-FIELD\n    12\t  imports INT\n    13\t  imports BOOL\n    14\t  imports LIST\n    15\t  imports K-EQUAL\n    16\t\n    17\t  syntax Int ::= \"#r\"        [function, total]\n    18\t               | \"#rJ\"       [function, total]\n    19\t               | \"#k256P\"    [function, total]\n    20\t               | \"#k256N\"    [function, total]\n    21\t               | \"#p256P\"    [function, total]\n    22\t               | \"#p256N\"    [function, total]\n    23\t               | \"#c25519P\"  [function, total]\n    24\t               | \"#c25519L\"  [function, total]\n    25\t  rule #r       => 52435875175126190479447740508185965837690552500527637822603658699938581184513\n    26\t  rule #rJ      => 6554484396890773809930967563523245729705921265872317281365359162392183254199\n    27\t  rule #k256P   => 115792089237316195423570985008687907853269984665640564039457584007908834671663\n    28\t  rule #k256N   => 115792089237316195423570985008687907852837564279074904382605163141518161494337\n    29\t  rule #p256P   => 115792089210356248762697446949407573530086143415290314195533631308867097853951\n    30\t  rule #p256N   => 115792089210356248762697446949407573529996955224135760342422259061068512044369\n    31\t  rule #c25519P => 57896044618658097711785492504343953926634992332820282019728792003956564819949\n    32\t  rule #c25519L => 7237005577332262213973186563042994240857116359379907606001950938285454250989\n    33\t\n    34\t  syntax Int ::= fmod(Int, Int)         [function, total]\n    35\t               | fadd(Int, Int, Int)    [function, total]\n    36\t               | fsub(Int, Int, Int)    [function, total]\n    37\t               | fmul(Int, Int, Int)    [function, total]\n    38\t               | fneg(Int, Int)         [function, total]\n    39\t               | finv(Int, Int)         [function, total]   // inverse by Fermat; finv(0) = 0\n    40\t               | fdiv(Int, Int, Int)    [function, total]\n    41\t               | fpow(Int, Int, Int)    [function, total]\n    42\t               | fsq(Int, Int)          [function, total]\n    43\t  rule fmod(A, P)     => A modInt P\n    44\t  rule fadd(A, B, P)  => (A +Int B) modInt P\n    45\t  rule fsub(A, B, P)  => (A -Int B) modInt P\n    46\t  rule fmul(A, B, P)  => (A *Int B) modInt P\n    47\t  rule fneg(A, P)     => (0 -Int A) modInt P\n    48\t  rule finv(A, P)     => 0 requires A modInt P ==Int 0\n    49\t  rule finv(A, P)     => (A modInt P) ^%Int (P -Int 2) P requires A modInt P =/=Int 0\n    50\t  rule fdiv(A, B, P)  => fmul(A, finv(B, P), P)\n    51\t  rule fpow(A, E, P)  => (A modInt P) ^%Int E P requires E >=Int 0\n    52\t  rule fpow(_, E, _)  => 0 requires E <Int 0\n    53\t  rule fsq(A, P)      => fmul(A, A, P)\n    54\t\n    55\t  // Legendre symbol as 0, 1 or P-1 (i.e. -1); 0 counts as a residue, as in\n    56\t  // midnight-curves `ct_quadratic_non_residue` (legendre == -1).\n    57\t  syntax Int ::= legendre(Int, Int) [function, total]\n    58\t  rule legendre(A, P) => fpow(A, (P -Int 1) /Int 2, P)\n    59\t  syntax Bool ::= isQuadraticNonResidue(Int, Int) [function, total]\n    60\t  rule isQuadraticNonResidue(A, P) => legendre(A, P) ==Int P -Int 1\n    61\t\n    62\t  syntax Bool ::= isOddInt(Int) [function, total]\n    63\t  rule isOddInt(A) => A modInt 2 ==Int 1\n    64\t\n    65\t  // --- Square roots: Tonelli-Shanks ---------------------------------------\n    66\t  // fsqrt(A, P) is sqrtOk(X) with X*X = A mod P for some root, or noSqrt().\n    67\t  // Callers that need a specific root fix the parity themselves, as the Rust\n    68\t  // code does (Jubjub decompression, SVDW map).\n    69\t  syntax SqrtResult ::= sqrtOk(Int) | noSqrt()\n    70\t  syntax SqrtResult ::= fsqrt(Int, Int) [function, total]\n    71\t  rule fsqrt(A, P) => sqrtOk(0) requires A modInt P ==Int 0\n    72\t  rule fsqrt(A, P) => noSqrt() requires A modInt P =/=Int 0 andBool legendre(A, P) =/=Int 1\n    73\t  rule fsqrt(A, P) => #ts(A modInt P, P, #twoAdicity(P -Int 1, 0), #oddPart(P -Int 1), #nonResidue(P, 2))\n    74\t    requires A modInt P =/=Int 0 andBool legendre(A, P) ==Int 1\n    75\t\n    76\t  syntax Int ::= #twoAdicity(Int, Int) [function, total]   // #twoAdicity(N, 0) = s with N = 2^s * odd\n    77\t  rule #twoAdicity(N, S) => #twoAdicity(N /Int 2, S +Int 1) requires N >Int 0 andBool N modInt 2 ==Int 0\n    78\t  rule #twoAdicity(N, S) => S requires N <=Int 0 orBool N modInt 2 ==Int 1\n    79\t  syntax Int ::= #oddPart(Int) [function, total]\n    80\t  rule #oddPart(N) => #oddPart(N /Int 2) requires N >Int 0 andBool N modInt 2 ==Int 0\n    81\t  rule #oddPart(N) => N requires N <=Int 0 orBool N modInt 2 ==Int 1\n    82\t  syntax Int ::= #nonResidue(Int, Int) [function, total]   // smallest quadratic non-residue >= Z\n    83\t  rule #nonResidue(P, Z) => Z requires isQuadraticNonResidue(Z, P)\n    84\t  rule #nonResidue(P, Z) => #nonResidue(P, Z +Int 1) requires notBool isQuadraticNonResidue(Z, P) andBool Z <Int P\n    85\t  rule #nonResidue(P, Z) => 0 requires Z >=Int P\n    86\t\n    87\t  // #ts(A, P, S, Q, Z): standard loop with M = S, c = Z^Q, t = A^Q, R = A^((Q+1)/2)\n    88\t  syntax SqrtResult ::= #ts(Int, Int, Int, Int, Int) [function, total]\n    89\t  rule #ts(A, P, S, Q, Z) => #tsLoop(P, S, fpow(Z, Q, P), fpow(A, Q, P), fpow(A, (Q +Int 1) /Int 2, P))\n    90\t  syntax SqrtResult ::= #tsLoop(Int, Int, Int, Int, Int) [function, total]   // (P, M, c, t, R)\n    91\t  rule #tsLoop(_, _, _, 0, _) => noSqrt()\n    92\t  rule #tsLoop(_, _, _, 1, R) => sqrtOk(R)\n    93\t  rule #tsLoop(P, M, C, T, R) => #tsStep(P, M, C, T, R, #tsOrder(P, T, 0, M))\n    94\t    requires T =/=Int 0 andBool T =/=Int 1\n    95\t  // least i with t^(2^i) = 1\n    96\t  syntax Int ::= #tsOrder(Int, Int, Int, Int) [function, total]\n    97\t  rule #tsOrder(_, 1, I, _) => I\n    98\t  rule #tsOrder(P, T, I, M) => #tsOrder(P, fsq(T, P), I +Int 1, M) requires T =/=Int 1 andBool I <Int M\n    99\t  rule #tsOrder(_, T, I, M) => I requires T =/=Int 1 andBool I >=Int M\n   100\t  syntax SqrtResult ::= #tsStep(Int, Int, Int, Int, Int, Int) [function, total]\n   101\t  rule #tsStep(P, M, C, T, R, I) => noSqrt() requires I >=Int M\n   102\t  rule #tsStep(P, M, C, T, R, I) => #tsLoop(P, I, fsq(fpow(C, 2 ^Int (M -Int I -Int 1), P), P),\n   103\t                                            fmul(T, fsq(fpow(C, 2 ^Int (M -Int I -Int 1), P), P), P),\n   104\t                                            fmul(R, fpow(C, 2 ^Int (M -Int I -Int 1), P), P))\n   105\t    requires I <Int M\n   106\t\n   107\t  // --- Bit and byte helpers ------------------------------------------------\n   108\t  // Little-endian bit I of A (0 or 1).\n   109\t  syntax Int ::= bitAt(Int, Int) [function, total]\n   110\t  rule bitAt(A, I) => (A >>Int I) &Int 1 requires I >=Int 0 andBool A >=Int 0\n   111\t  rule bitAt(_, _) => 0 [owise]\n   112\t  // Low N bits and the rest.\n   113\t  syntax Int ::= lowBits(Int, Int) [function, total]\n   114\t  rule lowBits(A, N) => A &Int ((1 <<Int N) -Int 1) requires N >=Int 0 andBool A >=Int 0\n   115\t  rule lowBits(_, _) => 0 [owise]\n   116\t  syntax Int ::= highBits(Int, Int) [function, total]   // A >> N\n   117\t  rule highBits(A, N) => A >>Int N requires N >=Int 0 andBool A >=Int 0\n   118\t  rule highBits(_, _) => 0 [owise]\n   119\t  syntax Bool ::= fitsBits(Int, Int) [function, total]   // 0 <= A < 2^N\n   120\t  rule fitsBits(A, N) => A >=Int 0 andBool A <Int (1 <<Int N) requires N >=Int 0\n   121\t  rule fitsBits(_, _) => false [owise]\n   122\tendmodule\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba experiments/zkir-k/tools/diff_test.py; nl -ba experiments/zkir-k/tools/zkir_run.py | sed -n '1,210p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"Oracle 1: differential test of the K semantics against the Rust crate.\n     2\t\n     3\tFor every version-3 program in the corpus:\n     4\t  1. draw raw inputs of the declared types (seeded per program);\n     5\t  2. run the K semantics in generation mode until the transcript needs are\n     6\t     stable (public/private transcript values of the requested types are\n     7\t     appended, impact values become public_transcript_inputs, and the\n     8\t     communications commitment is taken from the run);\n     9\t  3. run the real K semantics and the Rust `preprocess` (zkir-oracle) on the\n    10\t     same preimage and compare status, memory (variant and encoding of every\n    11\t     register), public inputs and skips;\n    12\t  4. repeat step 3 with one perturbed preimage (first raw input replaced), so\n    13\t     that error paths are compared too.\n    14\t\n    15\tUsage: uv run --group zkir-k python experiments/zkir-k/tools/diff_test.py [--only SUBSTR] [--seed N]\n    16\tExit 0 iff every comparison agrees.\n    17\t\"\"\"\n    18\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n    19\t\n    20\timport argparse\n    21\timport json\n    22\timport random\n    23\timport subprocess\n    24\timport sys\n    25\timport tempfile\n    26\timport time\n    27\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    28\t\n    29\tsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\n    30\timport zkir_kast  # noqa: E402\n    31\timport zkir_values as zv  # noqa: E402\n    32\tfrom zkir_run import Runner  # noqa: E402\n    33\t\n    34\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    35\tROOT = HERE.parent\n    36\tREPO = ROOT.parent.parent\n    37\tORACLE = Path.home() / 'Moriarty/repos/_build/ledger-92e8bdd3/target/release/zkir-oracle'\n    38\tORACLE_EXT = Path.home() / 'Moriarty/repos/_build/midnight-zkir-2ffe2d1/target/release/zkir-oracle'\n    39\t\n    40\tCORPORA = {\n    41\t    'ledger9-92e8bdd3-tests': ROOT / 'corpus' / 'ledger9-92e8bdd3-tests',\n    42\t    'midnight-zkir-2ffe2d1-precompiles': ROOT / 'corpus' / 'midnight-zkir-2ffe2d1-precompiles',\n    43\t    'moriarty-compact-escrow': REPO / 'experiments' / 'moriarty-compact-escrow' / 'output' / 'zkir',\n    44\t    'moriarty-core-swap': REPO / 'experiments' / 'moriarty-core-swap' / 'output' / 'zkir',\n    45\t    'handmade': ROOT / 'corpus' / 'handmade',\n    46\t}\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\tORACLE_BIN = ORACLE\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\tdef oracle(program: Path, preimage: dict) -> dict:\n    53\t    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile('w', suffix='.json', delete=False) as f:\n    54\t        json.dump(preimage, f)\n    55\t    res = subprocess.run([str(ORACLE_BIN), str(program), f.name], capture_output=True, text=True)\n    56\t    if res.returncode != 0:\n    57\t        return {'status': 'oracle-failed', 'error': res.stderr[-500:]}\n    58\t    return json.loads(res.stdout)\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\tdef strs(xs):\n    62\t    return [str(x) for x in xs]\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\tdef build_preimage(runner: Runner, program, doc: dict, rng: random.Random, small: bool, seed_pre: dict | None = None) -> tuple[dict, int]:\n    66\t    gen = zv.small_encoded if small else zv.random_encoded\n    67\t    inputs = [x for entry in doc['inputs'] for x in gen(entry['type'], rng)]\n    68\t    rand = rng.randrange(zv.R)\n    69\t    pre = {'inputs': strs(inputs), 'binding_input': str(rng.randrange(zv.R)),\n    70\t           'private_transcript': [], 'public_transcript_inputs': [], 'public_transcript_outputs': []}\n    71\t    if seed_pre:\n    72\t        # the crate's own test values, when they are literals (manifest test_preimage)\n    73\t        for key in ('inputs', 'private_transcript', 'public_transcript_outputs', 'binding_input'):\n    74\t            if key in seed_pre:\n    75\t                pre[key] = seed_pre[key]\n    76\t    if doc['do_communications_commitment']:\n    77\t        pre['communications_commitment'] = ['0', str(rand)]\n    78\t    passes = 0\n    79\t    for _ in range(8):\n    80\t        passes += 1\n    81\t        res = runner.run(program, pre, gen=True)\n    82\t        if res['status'] == 'krun-failed':\n    83\t            raise RuntimeError(res['error'])\n    84\t        needs = res['needs']\n    85\t        new_out = [t for kind, t in needs if kind == 'pubOut']\n    86\t        new_priv = [t for kind, t in needs if kind == 'priv']\n    87\t        pre['public_transcript_inputs'] = strs(x for kind, x in needs if kind == 'pubIn')\n    88\t        comm = [x for kind, x in needs if kind == 'comm']\n    89\t        if comm:\n    90\t            pre['communications_commitment'] = [str(comm[0]), str(rand)]\n    91\t        if not new_out and not new_priv:\n    92\t            break\n    93\t        pre['public_transcript_outputs'] += strs(x for t in new_out for x in gen(t, rng))\n    94\t        pre['private_transcript'] += strs(x for t in new_priv for x in gen(t, rng))\n    95\t    return pre, passes\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\tdef compare(k: dict, r: dict) -> list[str]:\n    99\t    diffs = []\n   100\t    if k['status'] != r['status']:\n   101\t        return [f\"status K={k['status']} ({k.get('error', '')[:80]}) Rust={r['status']} ({r.get('error', '')[:80]})\"]\n   102\t    if k['status'] != 'ok':\n   103\t        return diffs\n   104\t    if k['pis'] != r['pis']:\n   105\t        diffs.append(f\"pis differ: K={k['pis'][:6]} Rust={r['pis'][:6]}\")\n   106\t    if k['pi_skips'] != r['pi_skips']:\n   107\t        diffs.append(f\"pi_skips differ: K={k['pi_skips']} Rust={r['pi_skips']}\")\n   108\t    km, rm = k['memory'], r['memory']\n   109\t    for name in sorted(set(km) | set(rm)):\n   110\t        if name not in km:\n   111\t            diffs.append(f'{name}: missing in K')\n   112\t        elif name not in rm:\n   113\t            diffs.append(f'{name}: missing in Rust')\n   114\t        elif km[name] != rm[name]:\n   115\t            diffs.append(f\"{name}: K={km[name]} Rust={rm[name]}\")\n   116\t    return diffs\n   117\t\n   118\t\n   119\tdef main() -> int:\n   120\t    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n   121\t    ap.add_argument('--only', default='')\n   122\t    ap.add_argument('--seed', type=int, default=2026)\n   123\t    ap.add_argument('--no-perturb', action='store_true')\n   124\t    ap.add_argument('--attempts', type=int, default=8)\n   125\t    ap.add_argument('--ext', action='store_true', help='ZKIR-EXT definition, midnight-zkir 2ffe2d1 oracle and corpus')\n   126\t    args = ap.parse_args()\n   127\t    global ORACLE_BIN, CORPORA\n   128\t    if args.ext:\n   129\t        ORACLE_BIN = ORACLE_EXT\n   130\t        CORPORA = {\n   131\t            'midnight-zkir-2ffe2d1-tests': ROOT / 'corpus' / 'midnight-zkir-2ffe2d1-tests',\n   132\t            'midnight-zkir-2ffe2d1-precompiles': ROOT / 'corpus' / 'midnight-zkir-2ffe2d1-precompiles',\n   133\t            'handmade': ROOT / 'corpus' / 'handmade',\n   134\t        }\n   135\t    runner = Runner(ext=args.ext)\n   136\t    rows = []\n   137\t    failures = 0\n   138\t    t0 = time.time()\n   139\t    for corpus, directory in CORPORA.items():\n   140\t        for path in sorted(directory.glob('*.zkir')):\n   141\t            if args.only and args.only not in path.name:\n   142\t                continue\n   143\t            doc = json.loads(path.read_text())\n   144\t            if doc.get('version', {}).get('major') != 3:\n   145\t                continue\n   146\t            try:\n   147\t                program = zkir_kast.load_program(path, ext=args.ext)\n   148\t            except zkir_kast.ZkirFormatError:\n   149\t                continue   # rejected before preprocess by both sides\n   150\t            rng = random.Random(f'{args.seed}:{path.name}')\n   151\t            manifest = directory / 'manifest.json'\n   152\t            seed_pre = None\n   153\t            if manifest.exists():\n   154\t                for entry in json.loads(manifest.read_text()).get('programs', []):\n   155\t                    if entry['file'] == path.name:\n   156\t                        seed_pre = entry.get('test_preimage')\n   157\t            # Up to MAX_ATTEMPTS preimages with small native inputs; stop after the\n   158\t            # first one both sides accept. Every attempt is compared.\n   159\t            t1 = time.time()\n   160\t            for attempt in range(args.attempts):\n   161\t                try:\n   162\t                    pre, passes = build_preimage(runner, program, doc, rng, small=True, seed_pre=seed_pre if attempt == 0 else None)\n   163\t                except RuntimeError as e:\n   164\t                    rows.append((corpus, path.name, f'gen{attempt}', 'krun failed', [str(e)[-300:]]))\n   165\t                    failures += 1\n   166\t                    break\n   167\t                k = runner.run(program, pre)\n   168\t                r = oracle(path, pre)\n   169\t                diffs = compare(k, r)\n   170\t                failures += bool(diffs)\n   171\t                note = ''\n   172\t                if k['status'] == 'error':\n   173\t                    same = k.get('error', '')[:20] == r.get('error', '')[:20]\n   174\t                    note = f\" msg K='{k.get('error', '')[:70]}'\" + ('' if same else f\" Rust='{r.get('error', '')[:70]}'\")\n   175\t                viol = k.get('violations', [])\n   176\t                vnote = f\" verdicts={k.get('verdicts', 0)}\" + (f\" NON-HOLDING={len(viol)}: \" + '; '.join(f'{o}[{m}] {g[:50]}' for o, m, g in viol[:3]) if viol else '')\n   177\t                rows.append((corpus, path.name, f'run{attempt}', f\"K={k['status']} Rust={r['status']} regs={len(k.get('memory', {}))} pis={len(k.get('pis', []))} passes={passes} {time.time() - t1:.1f}s{note}{vnote}\", diffs))\n   178\t                if k['status'] == 'ok' and r['status'] == 'ok':\n   179\t                    if not args.no_perturb and pre['inputs']:\n   180\t                        pert = json.loads(json.dumps(pre))\n   181\t                        pert['inputs'][0] = str(rng.randrange(zv.R))\n   182\t                        k2 = runner.run(program, pert)\n   183\t                        r2 = oracle(path, pert)\n   184\t                        d2 = compare(k2, r2)\n   185\t                        failures += bool(d2)\n   186\t                        rows.append((corpus, path.name, 'perturbed', f\"K={k2['status']} Rust={r2['status']} regs={len(k2.get('memory', {}))}\", d2))\n   187\t                    break\n   188\t    for corpus, name, label, summary, diffs in rows:\n   189\t        print(f\"{'PASS' if not diffs else 'FAIL'}  {corpus:34} {name:52} {label:9} {summary}\")\n   190\t        for d in diffs[:8]:\n   191\t            print(f'        {d}')\n   192\t    oks = sum(1 for r in rows if r[3].startswith('K=ok Rust=ok'))\n   193\t    print(f'\\n{len(rows)} comparisons ({oks} successful runs), {len(rows) - failures} agree, {failures} disagree, {time.time() - t0:.0f}s')\n   194\t    return 1 if failures else 0\n   195\t\n   196\t\n   197\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   198\t    sys.exit(main())\n     1\t\"\"\"Run a ZKIR v3 program through the K semantics (ZKIR-VM) and read the result.\n     2\t\n     3\t`run_job(program_path, preimage)` builds job(Program, Preimage), runs krun on\n     4\tthe ZKIR definition, and returns a dict shaped like the Rust oracle's output:\n     5\t  {status: 'ok'|'error', error?: str, memory: {id: {variant, encoded}},\n     6\t   pis: [str], pi_skips: [None|int], cursors: (pubIn, pubOut, priv),\n     7\t   constraints: int}\n     8\tMemory values are re-encoded on the Python side with the same encoding as\n     9\t`encode_offcircuit` (the encodings are unit-tested against K in unit_values.py).\n    10\t\n    11\tUsage: zkir_run.py FILE.zkir PREIMAGE.json [--definition DIR]\n    12\t\"\"\"\n    13\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n    14\t\n    15\timport argparse\n    16\timport json\n    17\timport sys\n    18\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    19\tfrom typing import Any\n    20\t\n    21\tfrom pyk.kast.inner import KApply, KInner, KSort, KToken, top_down\n    22\tfrom pyk.kast.prelude.kint import intToken\n    23\tfrom pyk.kore.parser import KoreParser\n    24\tfrom pyk.ktool.krun import KRun\n    25\t\n    26\tsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\n    27\timport zkir_kast  # noqa: E402\n    28\t\n    29\tR = 52435875175126190479447740508185965837690552500527637822603658699938581184513\n    30\tRJ = 6554484396890773809930967563523245729705921265872317281365359162392183254199\n    31\tK256P = 2**256 - 2**32 - 977\n    32\tK256N = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFEBAAEDCE6AF48A03BBFD25E8CD0364141\n    33\tP256P = 0xFFFFFFFF00000001000000000000000000000000FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF\n    34\tP256N = 0xFFFFFFFF00000000FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFBCE6FAADA7179E84F3B9CAC2FC632551\n    35\tC25519P = 2**255 - 19\n    36\tC25519L = 2**252 + 27742317777372353535851937790883648493\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\tdef default_definition() -> Path:\n    40\t    return Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / 'semantics' / 'zkir-kompiled'\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\tdef default_ext_definition() -> Path:\n    44\t    return Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / 'semantics' / 'zkir-ext-kompiled'\n    45\t\n    46\t\n    47\t# --- preimage term ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n    48\t\n    49\tdef klist(items: list[KInner]) -> KInner:\n    50\t    t: KInner = KApply('.List')\n    51\t    for it in reversed(items):\n    52\t        t = KApply('_List_', [KApply('ListItem', [it]), t])\n    53\t    return t\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\tdef ints(values) -> KInner:\n    57\t    return klist([intToken(int(v)) for v in values])\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\tdef preimage_term(p: dict[str, Any]) -> KInner:\n    61\t    cc = p.get('communications_commitment')\n    62\t    comm = KApply('noComm') if cc is None else KApply('comm', [intToken(int(cc[0])), intToken(int(cc[1]))])\n    63\t    return KApply('preimage', [\n    64\t        ints(p.get('inputs', [])),\n    65\t        intToken(int(p.get('binding_input', 0))),\n    66\t        comm,\n    67\t        ints(p.get('private_transcript', [])),\n    68\t        ints(p.get('public_transcript_inputs', [])),\n    69\t        ints(p.get('public_transcript_outputs', [])),\n    70\t    ])\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\t# --- result extraction --------------------------------------------------------------------\n    74\t\n    75\tdef find_cell(term: KInner, name: str) -> KInner:\n    76\t    found: list[KInner] = []\n    77\t\n    78\t    def visit(t: KInner) -> KInner:\n    79\t        if isinstance(t, KApply) and t.label.name == name:\n    80\t            found.append(t.args[0])\n    81\t        return t\n    82\t\n    83\t    top_down(visit, term)\n    84\t    if not found:\n    85\t        raise KeyError(name)\n    86\t    return found[0]\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\tdef list_items(term: KInner) -> list[KInner]:\n    90\t    items: list[KInner] = []\n    91\t\n    92\t    def walk(t: KInner) -> None:\n    93\t        if isinstance(t, KApply):\n    94\t            if t.label.name == '_List_':\n    95\t                for a in t.args:\n    96\t                    walk(a)\n    97\t            elif t.label.name == 'ListItem':\n    98\t                items.append(t.args[0])\n    99\t            elif t.label.name == '.List':\n   100\t                pass\n   101\t            else:\n   102\t                raise ValueError(f'not a list: {t.label.name}')\n   103\t    walk(term)\n   104\t    return items\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\tdef map_items(term: KInner) -> list[tuple[KInner, KInner]]:\n   108\t    items: list[tuple[KInner, KInner]] = []\n   109\t\n   110\t    def walk(t: KInner) -> None:\n   111\t        if isinstance(t, KApply):\n   112\t            if t.label.name == '_Map_':\n   113\t                for a in t.args:\n   114\t                    walk(a)\n   115\t            elif t.label.name == '_|->_':\n   116\t                items.append((t.args[0], t.args[1]))\n   117\t            elif t.label.name == '.Map':\n   118\t                pass\n   119\t            else:\n   120\t                raise ValueError(f'not a map: {t.label.name}')\n   121\t    walk(term)\n   122\t    return items\n   123\t\n   124\t\n   125\tdef tok_int(t: KInner) -> int:\n   126\t    assert isinstance(t, KToken), t\n   127\t    return int(t.token)\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\tdef tok_str(t: KInner) -> str:\n   131\t    assert isinstance(t, KToken) and t.sort.name == 'String', t\n   132\t    return json.loads(t.token)\n   133\t\n   134\t\n   135\t_ESC = {'t': 9, 'n': 10, 'r': 13, 'f': 12, '\"': 34, '\\\\': 92}\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\tdef tok_bytes(t: KInner) -> bytes:\n   139\t    assert isinstance(t, KToken) and t.sort.name == 'Bytes', t\n   140\t    s = t.token\n   141\t    assert s.startswith('b\"') and s.endswith('\"'), s\n   142\t    body = s[2:-1]\n   143\t    out = bytearray()\n   144\t    i = 0\n   145\t    while i < len(body):\n   146\t        ch = body[i]\n   147\t        if ch == '\\\\':\n   148\t            nxt = body[i + 1]\n   149\t            if nxt == 'x':\n   150\t                out.append(int(body[i + 2:i + 4], 16))\n   151\t                i += 4\n   152\t            elif nxt == 'u':\n   153\t                out.append(int(body[i + 2:i + 6], 16))\n   154\t                i += 6\n   155\t            else:\n   156\t                out.append(_ESC[nxt])\n   157\t                i += 2\n   158\t        else:\n   159\t            out.append(ord(ch))\n   160\t            i += 1\n   161\t    return bytes(out)\n   162\t\n   163\t\n   164\tdef enc_foreign(x: int, mod: int, log2: int, nb: int) -> list[int]:\n   165\t    e = (x - 1) % mod\n   166\t    per = 254 // log2\n   167\t    out = []\n   168\t    left = nb\n   169\t    while left > 0:\n   170\t        take = min(left, per)\n   171\t        out.append(e & ((1 << (log2 * take)) - 1))\n   172\t        e >>= log2 * take\n   173\t        left -= take\n   174\t    return out\n   175\t\n   176\t\n   177\tdef point(t: KInner):\n   178\t    assert isinstance(t, KApply)\n   179\t    if t.label.name == 'inf':\n   180\t        return None\n   181\t    assert t.label.name == 'pt', t\n   182\t    return (tok_int(t.args[0]), tok_int(t.args[1]))\n   183\t\n   184\t\n   185\tdef enc_chunks(b: bytes) -> list[int]:\n   186\t    return [int.from_bytes(b[i:i + 31], 'little') for i in range(0, len(b), 31)]\n   187\t\n   188\t\n   189\tdef encode_value(t: KInner, ext: bool = False) -> tuple[str, list[int]]:\n   190\t    assert isinstance(t, KApply), t\n   191\t    lbl = t.label.name\n   192\t    a = t.args\n   193\t    match lbl:\n   194\t        case 'nativeV':\n   195\t            return 'Native', [tok_int(a[0])]\n   196\t        case 'bytes32V':\n   197\t            b = tok_bytes(a[0])\n   198\t            return ('Bytes' if ext else 'Bytes32'), [int.from_bytes(b[:31], 'little'), b[31]]\n   199\t        case 'boolV':\n   200\t            return 'Bool', [1 if (a[0].token if isinstance(a[0], KToken) else a[0].label.name) == 'true' else 0]\n   201\t        case 'byteV':\n   202\t            return 'Byte', [tok_int(a[0])]\n   203\t        case 'bytesV':\n   204\t            return 'Bytes', enc_chunks(tok_bytes(a[0]))\n   205\t        case 'jubjubPointV':\n   206\t            p = point(a[0]) or (0, 1)\n   207\t            return 'JubjubPoint', [p[0], p[1]]\n   208\t        case 'jubjubScalarV':\n   209\t            return 'JubjubScalar', [tok_int(a[0])]\n   210\t        case 'secp256k1PointV' | 'secp256r1PointV':\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba experiments/zkir-k/semantics/zkir-constraints.k | sed -n '1,205p'; nl -ba experiments/zkir-k/semantics/zkir-vm.k | sed -n '1,205p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba experiments/zkir-k/semantics/zkir-constraints.k | sed -n '1,205p'; nl -ba experiments/zkir-k/semantics/zkir-vm.k | sed -n '1,205p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t// Constraint checker (oracle 2, plan CLM-0716 item 2): does the witness in\n     2\t// <mem> satisfy the in-circuit relation of every emitted constraint?\n     3\t//\n     4\t// A constraint is instruction-level: gate(I) is the relation that\n     5\t// `Relation::circuit` in ir_vm.rs (midnight-ledger 92e8bdd3) and the\n     6\t// `*_incircuit` functions of ir_instructions/*.rs enforce for instruction I,\n     7\t// read off the chip calls they make; piGate(i, g, x) is pi[i] = g ? x : 0 with\n     8\t// g boolean; piFixed(i, _) pins the binding input and the commitment. The\n     9\t// relation is evaluated with concrete values, so this establishes only that the\n    10\t// honest witness satisfies the constraints (completeness), never that no other\n    11\t// witness does (CLM-0721).\n    12\t//\n    13\t// Outcomes per constraint:\n    14\t//   holds()            the relation is satisfied\n    15\t//   violated(msg)      the relation is not satisfied (an unsatisfiable circuit)\n    16\t//   synthErr(msg)      the circuit cannot be built: an in-circuit dispatch has\n    17\t//                      no arm for these types (Error::Synthesis) or a chip the\n    18\t//                      gate needs is not initialised (`used_chips`, finding 13)\n    19\t//   unknown(msg)       a register the gate reads is absent (witness stopped early)\n    20\t//\n    21\t// Chip gating follows `IrSource::used_chips`: a foreign chip is initialised only\n    22\t// when its types occur among the program inputs or public/private inputs, the\n    23\t// Jubjub chip additionally by hash_to_curve, Poseidon by transient_hash,\n    24\t// hash_to_curve or the communications commitment, SHA-256 by persistent_hash,\n    25\t// Keccak by keccak256. from_bytes32 does not initialise anything (finding 13).\n    26\trequires \"zkir-ops.k\"\n    27\t\n    28\tmodule ZKIR-CONSTRAINTS\n    29\t  imports ZKIR-OPS\n    30\t  imports ZKIR-WF\n    31\t  imports MAP\n    32\t  imports SET\n    33\t\n    34\t  syntax Constraint ::= gate(Instr)                       [symbol(gate)]\n    35\t                      | piGate(Int, Operand, Operand)     [symbol(piGate)]\n    36\t                      | piFixed(Int, Operand)             [symbol(piFixed)]\n    37\t  syntax Outcome ::= holds() [symbol(holds)] | violated(String) [symbol(violated)]\n    38\t                   | synthErr(String) [symbol(synthErr)] | unknown(String) [symbol(unknown)]\n    39\t  syntax Verdict ::= verdict(Constraint, Outcome) [symbol(verdict)]\n    40\t\n    41\t  // --- Chips -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n    42\t  syntax Set ::= usedChips(Program) [function, total]\n    43\t  rule usedChips(program(_, Ins, _, DoComm, Is))\n    44\t    => #chipsOfTypes(#inputTypes(Ins) #ioTypes(Is)) |Set #chipsOfInstrs(Is) |Set #commChip(DoComm)\n    45\t  syntax Set ::= #commChip(Bool) [function, total]\n    46\t  rule #commChip(true) => SetItem(\"poseidon\")\n    47\t  rule #commChip(false) => .Set\n    48\t  syntax List ::= #inputTypes(TypedIds) [function, total]\n    49\t  rule #inputTypes(.TypedIds) => .List\n    50\t  rule #inputTypes((typedId(_, T), Rest)) => ListItem(T) #inputTypes(Rest)\n    51\t  syntax List ::= #ioTypes(Instrs) [function, total]\n    52\t  rule #ioTypes(.Instrs) => .List\n    53\t  rule #ioTypes((publicInput(_, T, _) ; Is)) => ListItem(T) #ioTypes(Is)\n    54\t  rule #ioTypes((privateInput(_, T, _) ; Is)) => ListItem(T) #ioTypes(Is)\n    55\t  rule #ioTypes((_ ; Is)) => #ioTypes(Is) [owise]\n    56\t  syntax Set ::= #chipsOfTypes(List) [function, total]\n    57\t  rule #chipsOfTypes(.List) => .Set\n    58\t  rule #chipsOfTypes(ListItem(T:IrType) L) => chipOfType(T) |Set #chipsOfTypes(L)\n    59\t  rule #chipsOfTypes(ListItem(_) L) => #chipsOfTypes(L) [owise]\n    60\t  syntax Set ::= #chipsOfInstrs(Instrs) [function, total]\n    61\t  rule #chipsOfInstrs(.Instrs) => .Set\n    62\t  rule #chipsOfInstrs((hashToCurve(_, _) ; Is)) => (SetItem(\"jubjub\") SetItem(\"poseidon\")) |Set #chipsOfInstrs(Is)\n    63\t  rule #chipsOfInstrs((transientHash(_, _) ; Is)) => SetItem(\"poseidon\") |Set #chipsOfInstrs(Is)\n    64\t  rule #chipsOfInstrs((persistentHash(_, _, _) ; Is)) => SetItem(\"sha2_256\") |Set #chipsOfInstrs(Is)\n    65\t  rule #chipsOfInstrs((keccak256(_, _, _) ; Is)) => SetItem(\"keccak_256\") |Set #chipsOfInstrs(Is)\n    66\t  rule #chipsOfInstrs((_ ; Is)) => #chipsOfInstrs(Is) [owise]\n    67\t\n    68\t  // chip needed to hold a value of a type (\"\" = none)\n    69\t  syntax Set ::= chipOfType(IrType) [function, total]\n    70\t  rule chipOfType(jubjubPoint())     => SetItem(\"jubjub\")\n    71\t  rule chipOfType(jubjubScalar())    => SetItem(\"jubjub\")\n    72\t  rule chipOfType(secp256k1Point())  => SetItem(\"secp256k1\")\n    73\t  rule chipOfType(secp256k1Base())   => SetItem(\"secp256k1\")\n    74\t  rule chipOfType(secp256k1Scalar()) => SetItem(\"secp256k1\")\n    75\t  rule chipOfType(secp256r1Point())  => SetItem(\"p256\")\n    76\t  rule chipOfType(secp256r1Base())   => SetItem(\"p256\")\n    77\t  rule chipOfType(secp256r1Scalar()) => SetItem(\"p256\")\n    78\t  rule chipOfType(curve25519Point()) => SetItem(\"curve25519\")\n    79\t  rule chipOfType(curve25519Base())  => SetItem(\"curve25519\")\n    80\t  rule chipOfType(curve25519Scalar())=> SetItem(\"curve25519\")\n    81\t  rule chipOfType(_) => .Set [owise]\n    82\t\n    83\t  // --- Evaluation of all constraints --------------------------------------------------\n    84\t  // verdicts(constraints, mem, pi, chips, binding, commOpt)\n    85\t  syntax List ::= verdicts(List, Map, List, Set) [function, total]\n    86\t  rule verdicts(.List, _, _, _) => .List\n    87\t  rule verdicts(ListItem(C:Constraint) Cs, M, Pi, Chips) => ListItem(verdict(C, eval(C, M, Pi, Chips))) verdicts(Cs, M, Pi, Chips)\n    88\t  rule verdicts(ListItem(_) Cs, M, Pi, Chips) => verdicts(Cs, M, Pi, Chips) [owise]\n    89\t\n    90\t  syntax List ::= violations(List) [function, total]   // verdicts that are not holds()\n    91\t  rule violations(.List) => .List\n    92\t  rule violations(ListItem(verdict(_, holds())) Vs) => violations(Vs)\n    93\t  rule violations(ListItem(V) Vs) => ListItem(V) violations(Vs) [owise]\n    94\t\n    95\t  // --- Reading the witness ------------------------------------------------------------\n    96\t  syntax ValueResult ::= rd(Operand, Map) [function, total]\n    97\t  rule rd(imm(I), _) => vOk(native(I))\n    98\t  rule rd(var(X), M) => vOk({M[X]}:>Value) requires X in_keys(M)\n    99\t  rule rd(var(X), M) => vErr(\"register \" +String X +String \" is not in the witness\") requires notBool X in_keys(M)\n   100\t  syntax ValueResult ::= rdId(String, Map) [function, total]\n   101\t  rule rdId(X, M) => rd(var(X), M)\n   102\t\n   103\t  syntax Outcome ::= #need(ValueResult) [function, total]   // an absent register makes the outcome unknown\n   104\t  rule #need(vErr(S)) => unknown(S)\n   105\t  rule #need(vOk(_)) => holds()\n   106\t\n   107\t  syntax Outcome ::= #and(Outcome, Outcome) [function, total]   // first non-holds outcome wins\n   108\t  rule #and(holds(), O) => O\n   109\t  rule #and(O, _) => O requires O =/=K holds()\n   110\t\n   111\t  syntax Outcome ::= #chipFor(IrType, Set) [function, total]\n   112\t  rule #chipFor(T, Chips) => holds() requires chipOfType(T) <=Set Chips\n   113\t  rule #chipFor(T, Chips) => synthErr(\"chip not initialised for \" +String typeName(T)) requires notBool (chipOfType(T) <=Set Chips)\n   114\t  syntax Outcome ::= #chipsForValues(List, Set) [function, total]\n   115\t  rule #chipsForValues(.List, _) => holds()\n   116\t  rule #chipsForValues(ListItem(V:Value) L, Chips) => #and(#chipFor(typeOf(V), Chips), #chipsForValues(L, Chips))\n   117\t  rule #chipsForValues(ListItem(_) L, Chips) => #chipsForValues(L, Chips) [owise]\n   118\t\n   119\t  syntax Outcome ::= #native(ValueResult, String) [function, total]\n   120\t  rule #native(vErr(S), _) => unknown(S)\n   121\t  rule #native(vOk(native(_)), _) => holds()\n   122\t  rule #native(vOk(V), What) => synthErr(What +String \": cannot convert \" +String tn(V) +String \" to Native\") [owise]\n   123\t  syntax Outcome ::= #boolean(ValueResult, String) [function, total]\n   124\t  rule #boolean(vErr(S), _) => unknown(S)\n   125\t  rule #boolean(vOk(native(0)), _) => holds()\n   126\t  rule #boolean(vOk(native(1)), _) => holds()\n   127\t  rule #boolean(vOk(native(V)), What) => violated(What +String \" is not boolean: \" +String Int2String(V)) requires V =/=Int 0 andBool V =/=Int 1\n   128\t  rule #boolean(vOk(V), What) => synthErr(What +String \": cannot convert \" +String tn(V) +String \" to Native\") [owise]\n   129\t  syntax Outcome ::= #eqValues(ValueResult, ValueResult, String) [function, total]\n   130\t  rule #eqValues(vErr(S), _, _) => unknown(S)\n   131\t  rule #eqValues(vOk(_), vErr(S), _) => unknown(S)\n   132\t  rule #eqValues(vOk(A), vOk(B), _) => holds() requires A ==K B\n   133\t  rule #eqValues(vOk(A), vOk(B), What) => violated(What) requires A =/=K B\n   134\t  // expected value computed by an off-circuit function vs the register\n   135\t  syntax Outcome ::= #matches(ValueResult, ValueResult, String) [function, total]\n   136\t  rule #matches(vErr(S), _, What) => synthErr(What +String \": \" +String S)   // the in-circuit op is undefined on these types\n   137\t  rule #matches(vOk(_), vErr(S), _) => unknown(S)\n   138\t  rule #matches(vOk(A), vOk(B), _) => holds() requires A ==K B\n   139\t  rule #matches(vOk(A), vOk(B), What) => violated(What) requires A =/=K B\n   140\t  syntax Int ::= #int(ValueResult) [function, total]\n   141\t  rule #int(vOk(native(X))) => X\n   142\t  rule #int(_) => -1 [owise]\n   143\t\n   144\t  // --- Gates --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   145\t  syntax Outcome ::= eval(Constraint, Map, List, Set) [function, total]\n   146\t\n   147\t  rule eval(piFixed(_, _), _, _, _) => holds()\n   148\t  rule eval(piGate(I, G, X), M, Pi, _) => #and(#boolean(rd(G, M), \"impact guard\"), #and(#native(rd(X, M), \"impact\"), #piEq(I, rd(G, M), rd(X, M), Pi)))\n   149\t  syntax Outcome ::= #piEq(Int, ValueResult, ValueResult, List) [function, total]\n   150\t  rule #piEq(I, _, _, Pi) => violated(\"public input index \" +String Int2String(I) +String \" out of range\") requires I >=Int size(Pi)\n   151\t  rule #piEq(I, G, X, Pi) => holds() requires I <Int size(Pi) andBool {Pi[I]}:>Int ==Int #guarded(#int(G), #int(X))\n   152\t  rule #piEq(I, G, X, Pi) => violated(\"public input \" +String Int2String(I) +String \" differs from the guarded value\") requires I <Int size(Pi) andBool {Pi[I]}:>Int =/=Int #guarded(#int(G), #int(X))\n   153\t  syntax Int ::= #guarded(Int, Int) [function, total]\n   154\t  rule #guarded(1, X) => X\n   155\t  rule #guarded(_, _) => 0 [owise]\n   156\t\n   157\t  // assert: cond != 0 (finding 2: booleanity is not enforced in circuit)\n   158\t  rule eval(gate(assert(C)), M, _, _) => #and(#native(rd(C, M), \"assert\"), #nonZero(rd(C, M)))\n   159\t  syntax Outcome ::= #nonZero(ValueResult) [function, total]\n   160\t  rule #nonZero(vOk(native(0))) => violated(\"assert of zero\")\n   161\t  rule #nonZero(_) => holds() [owise]\n   162\t\n   163\t  rule eval(gate(constrainToBoolean(V)), M, _, _) => #boolean(rd(V, M), \"constrain_to_boolean\")\n   164\t  rule eval(gate(constrainBits(V, N)), M, _, _) => #and(#native(rd(V, M), \"constrain_bits\"), #bits(rd(V, M), N))\n   165\t  syntax Outcome ::= #bits(ValueResult, Int) [function, total]\n   166\t  rule #bits(vOk(native(X)), N) => holds() requires N >=Int #frBits orBool fitsBits(X, N)\n   167\t  rule #bits(vOk(native(X)), N) => violated(\"value does not fit in \" +String Int2String(N) +String \" bits\") requires N <Int #frBits andBool notBool fitsBits(X, N)\n   168\t  rule #bits(_, _) => holds() [owise]\n   169\t\n   170\t  // constrain_eq / test_eq / cond_select: in-circuit dispatch has no arm for\n   171\t  // JubjubScalar (constrain_eq, findings 7) nor Bytes32 / JubjubScalar (cond_select, finding 6)\n   172\t  rule eval(gate(constrainEq(A, B)), M, _, Chips) => #and(#need(rd(A, M)), #and(#need(rd(B, M)),\n   173\t      #and(#chipsForValues(#vals(rd(A, M), rd(B, M)), Chips), #and(#eqSupported(rd(A, M), rd(B, M), \"constrain_eq\"), #eqValues(rd(A, M), rd(B, M), \"constrain_eq fails\")))))\n   174\t  syntax List ::= #vals(ValueResult, ValueResult) [function, total]\n   175\t  rule #vals(vOk(A), vOk(B)) => ListItem(A) ListItem(B)\n   176\t  rule #vals(vOk(A), vErr(_)) => ListItem(A)\n   177\t  rule #vals(vErr(_), vOk(B)) => ListItem(B)\n   178\t  rule #vals(vErr(_), vErr(_)) => .List\n   179\t  syntax Outcome ::= #eqSupported(ValueResult, ValueResult, String) [function, total]\n   180\t  rule #eqSupported(vOk(A), vOk(B), What) => synthErr(\"Unsupported \" +String What +String \": \" +String tn(A) +String \" == \" +String tn(B)) requires notBool sameType(A, B)\n   181\t  rule #eqSupported(vOk(jubjubScalar(_)), vOk(jubjubScalar(_)), What) => synthErr(\"Unsupported \" +String What +String \": JubjubScalar == JubjubScalar\")\n   182\t  rule #eqSupported(vOk(bytes32(_)), vOk(bytes32(_)), \"cond_select\") => synthErr(\"Unsupported cond_select: Bytes32 ? Bytes32\")\n   183\t  rule #eqSupported(vOk(bytes32(_)), vOk(bytes32(_)), \"constrain_eq\") => holds()\n   184\t  rule #eqSupported(vOk(bytes32(_)), vOk(bytes32(_)), \"test_eq\") => holds()\n   185\t  rule #eqSupported(_, _, _) => holds() [owise]\n   186\t\n   187\t  rule eval(gate(testEq(A, B, O)), M, _, Chips) => #and(#need(rd(A, M)), #and(#need(rd(B, M)),\n   188\t      #and(#chipsForValues(#vals(rd(A, M), rd(B, M)), Chips), #and(#eqSupported(rd(A, M), rd(B, M), \"test_eq\"),\n   189\t      #matches(#bin2(rd(A, M), rd(B, M), \"test_eq\"), rdId(O, M), \"test_eq output\")))))\n   190\t  rule eval(gate(condSelect(Bit, A, B, O)), M, _, Chips) => #and(#boolean(rd(Bit, M), \"cond_select bit\"), #and(#need(rd(A, M)), #and(#need(rd(B, M)),\n   191\t      #and(#chipsForValues(#vals(rd(A, M), rd(B, M)), Chips), #and(#eqSupported(rd(A, M), rd(B, M), \"cond_select\"),\n   192\t      #matches(#selBit(#int(rd(Bit, M)), rd(A, M), rd(B, M)), rdId(O, M), \"cond_select output\"))))))\n   193\t  syntax ValueResult ::= #selBit(Int, ValueResult, ValueResult) [function, total]\n   194\t  rule #selBit(1, vOk(A), vOk(B)) => selectV(true, A, B)\n   195\t  rule #selBit(0, vOk(A), vOk(B)) => selectV(false, A, B)\n   196\t  rule #selBit(_, vOk(A), vOk(B)) => selectV(false, A, B) [owise]\n   197\t  rule #selBit(_, _, _) => vErr(\"missing\") [owise]\n   198\t\n   199\t  syntax ValueResult ::= #bin2(ValueResult, ValueResult, String) [function, total]\n   200\t  rule #bin2(vErr(S), _, _) => vErr(S)\n   201\t  rule #bin2(vOk(_), vErr(S), _) => vErr(S)\n   202\t  rule #bin2(vOk(A), vOk(B), \"add\") => addV(A, B)\n   203\t  rule #bin2(vOk(A), vOk(B), \"mul\") => mulV(A, B)\n   204\t  rule #bin2(vOk(A), vOk(B), \"test_eq\") => testEqV(A, B)\n   205\t  rule #bin2(vOk(A), vOk(B), \"ec_mul\") => ecMulV(A, B)\n     1\t// ZKIR v3 virtual machine: the witness computation (`IrSource::preprocess`,\n     2\t// zkir-v3/src/ir_vm.rs at midnight-ledger 92e8bdd3) and, in the same rewrite,\n     3\t// the constraint set that `Relation::circuit` would synthesise for the same\n     4\t// instruction (plan decisions CLM-0704 .. CLM-0706, CLM-0720).\n     5\t//\n     6\t// State (one cell per component of the seven-tuple on the VM wiki page):\n     7\t//   <mem>        registers, String |-> Value, write-once\n     8\t//   <pi>         public-input vector (binding input, optional commitment, impacts)\n     9\t//   <skips>      pi_skips: skipNone() for an active impact, skipSome(n) for an inactive one\n    10\t//   <pubInIdx>, <pubOutIdx>, <privIdx>   transcript cursors\n    11\t//   <outputs>    values returned by `output`, in order\n    12\t//   <constraints> instruction-level relations emitted by every instruction,\n    13\t//                whether or not the witness computation is still alive\n    14\t//   <status>     ok() or error(msg): the first witness failure freezes the\n    15\t//                witness cells; the remaining instructions still emit constraints\n    16\t//\n    17\t// A run is job(program, preimage). The preimage mirrors `ProofPreimage`.\n    18\trequires \"zkir-syntax.k\"\n    19\trequires \"zkir-ops.k\"\n    20\trequires \"zkir-constraints.k\"\n    21\t\n    22\tmodule ZKIR-VM-SYNTAX\n    23\t  imports ZKIR-SYNTAX\n    24\t  imports LIST\n    25\t  imports INT\n    26\t\n    27\t  syntax Preimage ::= preimage(List, Int, CommOpt, List, List, List) [symbol(preimage)]\n    28\t                      // inputs, binding_input, communications_commitment, private_transcript,\n    29\t                      // public_transcript_inputs, public_transcript_outputs\n    30\t  syntax CommOpt  ::= noComm()        [symbol(noComm)]\n    31\t                    | comm(Int, Int)  [symbol(comm)]    // (commitment, opening randomness)\n    32\t  syntax Job ::= job(Program, Preimage)    [symbol(job)]\n    33\t               | genJob(Program, Preimage) [symbol(genJob)]   // generation mode, see <genMode>\n    34\tendmodule\n    35\t\n    36\tmodule ZKIR-VM\n    37\t  imports ZKIR-VM-SYNTAX\n    38\t  imports ZKIR-WF\n    39\t  imports ZKIR-OPS\n    40\t  imports ZKIR-CONSTRAINTS\n    41\t  imports MAP\n    42\t  imports SET\n    43\t  imports K-EQUAL\n    44\t\n    45\t  syntax Status ::= ok() [symbol(ok)] | error(String) [symbol(error)]\n    46\t  syntax Skip   ::= skipNone() [symbol(skipNone)] | skipSome(Int) [symbol(skipSome)]\n    47\t\n    48\t  // Constraints (sort Constraint, ZKIR-CONSTRAINTS): the in-circuit relation\n    49\t  // of one instruction over register names and immediates; piGate(i, g, x)\n    50\t  // states pi[i] = g ? x : 0; piFixed pins the binding input and commitment.\n    51\t\n    52\t  configuration\n    53\t    <zkir>\n    54\t      <k> $PGM:Job </k>\n    55\t      <mem> .Map </mem>\n    56\t      <pi> .List </pi>\n    57\t      <skips> .List </skips>\n    58\t      <pubInIdx> 0 </pubInIdx>\n    59\t      <pubOutIdx> 0 </pubOutIdx>\n    60\t      <privIdx> 0 </privIdx>\n    61\t      <outputs> .List </outputs>\n    62\t      <outTypes> .IrTypes </outTypes>\n    63\t      <doComm> false </doComm>\n    64\t      <pre> preimage(.List, 0, noComm(), .List, .List, .List) </pre>\n    65\t      <constraints> .List </constraints>\n    66\t      <chips> .Set </chips>\n    67\t      <verdicts> .List </verdicts>\n    68\t      <deadPis> 0 </deadPis>\n    69\t      <genMode> false </genMode>\n    70\t      <needs> .List </needs>\n    71\t      <strictDecode> false </strictDecode>   // true for the ZKIR-EXT surface (canonical-form check on decoding)\n    72\t      <status> ok() </status>\n    73\t    </zkir>\n    74\t\n    75\t  // Generation mode (test harness only): a transcript that runs out yields the\n    76\t  // type's default value and records what was needed; impact values and the\n    77\t  // communications commitment are recorded instead of checked. The harness\n    78\t  // (tools/diff_test.py) uses this to build a consistent preimage before the\n    79\t  // real run.\n    80\t  syntax Need ::= needPubOut(IrType) [symbol(needPubOut)]\n    81\t                | needPriv(IrType)   [symbol(needPriv)]\n    82\t                | needPubIn(Int)     [symbol(needPubIn)]\n    83\t                | needComm(Int)      [symbol(needComm)]\n    84\t  rule <k> genJob(P, Pre) => job(P, Pre) ... </k> <genMode> _ => true </genMode>\n    85\t\n    86\t  // --- Start: decode inputs, seed the public-input vector ------------------------------\n    87\t  rule <k> job(program(Mi, Ins, Outs, DoComm, Is), Pre) => #loadInputs(decodeInputs(#preInputs(Pre), Ins, 0, Strict)) ~> #seedPi ~> Is ~> #verdicts </k>\n    88\t       <pre> _ => Pre </pre> <strictDecode> Strict </strictDecode>\n    89\t       <chips> _ => usedChips(program(Mi, Ins, Outs, DoComm, Is)) </chips>\n    90\t       <outTypes> _ => Outs </outTypes>\n    91\t       <doComm> _ => DoComm </doComm>\n    92\t\n    93\t  syntax List ::= #preInputs(Preimage) [function, total]\n    94\t  rule #preInputs(preimage(I, _, _, _, _, _)) => I\n    95\t  syntax Int ::= #preBinding(Preimage) [function, total]\n    96\t  rule #preBinding(preimage(_, B, _, _, _, _)) => B\n    97\t  syntax CommOpt ::= #preComm(Preimage) [function, total]\n    98\t  rule #preComm(preimage(_, _, C, _, _, _)) => C\n    99\t  syntax List ::= #prePrivate(Preimage) [function, total]\n   100\t  rule #prePrivate(preimage(_, _, _, P, _, _)) => P\n   101\t  syntax List ::= #prePubIn(Preimage) [function, total]\n   102\t  rule #prePubIn(preimage(_, _, _, _, P, _)) => P\n   103\t  syntax List ::= #prePubOut(Preimage) [function, total]\n   104\t  rule #prePubOut(preimage(_, _, _, _, _, P)) => P\n   105\t\n   106\t  syntax KItem ::= #loadInputs(DecodeMany) | \"#seedPi\" | #bind(List)\n   107\t  rule <k> #loadInputs(decManyErr(S)) => .K ... </k> <status> ok() => error(S) </status>\n   108\t  rule <k> #loadInputs(decManyOk(L)) => #bind(L) ... </k>\n   109\t  rule <k> #bind(.List) => .K ... </k>\n   110\t  rule <k> #bind(ListItem(binding(N, V)) L) => #bind(L) ... </k> <mem> M => M[N <- V] </mem>\n   111\t\n   112\t  // pis = [binding_input] ++ [commitment if do_communications_commitment]\n   113\t  rule <k> #seedPi => .K ... </k> <pre> Pre </pre> <doComm> false </doComm>\n   114\t       <pi> _ => ListItem(#preBinding(Pre)) </pi>\n   115\t       <constraints> Cs => Cs ListItem(piFixed(0, var(\"$binding\"))) </constraints>\n   116\t  rule <k> #seedPi => .K ... </k> <pre> Pre </pre> <doComm> true </doComm>\n   117\t       <pi> _ => ListItem(#preBinding(Pre)) ListItem(#commValue(#preComm(Pre))) </pi>\n   118\t       <constraints> Cs => Cs ListItem(piFixed(0, var(\"$binding\"))) ListItem(piFixed(1, var(\"$commitment\"))) </constraints>\n   119\t       <status> St => #requireComm(#preComm(Pre), St) </status>\n   120\t  syntax Int ::= #commValue(CommOpt) [function, total]\n   121\t  rule #commValue(comm(C, _)) => C\n   122\t  rule #commValue(noComm()) => 0\n   123\t  syntax Status ::= #requireComm(CommOpt, Status) [function, total]\n   124\t  rule #requireComm(noComm(), ok()) => error(\"Expected communications commitment\")\n   125\t  rule #requireComm(_, St) => St [owise]\n   126\t\n   127\t  // --- Instruction sequencing ------------------------------------------------------------\n   128\t  rule <k> (I:Instr ; Is:Instrs) => I ~> Is ... </k>\n   129\t  rule <k> .Instrs => #finish ... </k>\n   130\t\n   131\t  // Every instruction emits its constraint, then runs its witness half (if alive).\n   132\t  // The witness half is written as #exec(I); when the status is an error only\n   133\t  // the constraint half fires.\n   134\t  syntax KItem ::= #exec(Instr)\n   135\t  rule <k> I:Instr => #exec(I) ... </k> <constraints> Cs => Cs #constraintsOf(I) </constraints>\n   136\t    requires notBool isImpact(I)\n   137\t  rule <k> #exec(_) => .K ... </k> <status> error(_) </status>\n   138\t\n   139\t  syntax Bool ::= isImpact(Instr) [function, total]\n   140\t  rule isImpact(impact(_, _)) => true\n   141\t  rule isImpact(_) => false [owise]\n   142\t  syntax List ::= #constraintsOf(Instr) [function, total]\n   143\t  rule #constraintsOf(I) => ListItem(gate(I))\n   144\t\n   145\t  // impact: constraints reference absolute public-input positions, so they\n   146\t  // depend on how many public inputs precede them; with a dead witness the\n   147\t  // count continues from the constraint side (piIdx cell would be needed for\n   148\t  // full independence; here we use the length of <pi>, which is frozen on\n   149\t  // error, plus the impacts seen since). The dead-witness case is tracked by\n   150\t  // <deadPis>.\n   151\t  rule <k> impact(G, Xs) => #exec(impact(G, Xs)) ... </k>\n   152\t       <pi> Pi </pi> <deadPis> D </deadPis>\n   153\t       <constraints> Cs => Cs #piGates(size(Pi) +Int D, G, Xs) </constraints>\n   154\t  syntax List ::= #piGates(Int, Operand, Operands) [function, total]\n   155\t  rule #piGates(_, _, .Operands) => .List\n   156\t  rule #piGates(N, G, (X, Xs)) => ListItem(piGate(N, G, X)) #piGates(N +Int 1, G, Xs)\n   157\t\n   158\t  rule <k> #exec(impact(_, Xs)) => .K ... </k> <status> error(_) </status> <deadPis> D => D +Int lenOperands(Xs) </deadPis>\n   159\t    [priority(30)]\n   160\t\n   161\t  // --- Operand resolution ----------------------------------------------------------------\n   162\t  syntax ValueResult ::= resolve(Operand, Map) [function, total]\n   163\t  rule resolve(imm(I), _) => vOk(native(I))\n   164\t  rule resolve(var(X), M) => vOk({M[X]}:>Value) requires X in_keys(M)\n   165\t  rule resolve(var(X), M) => vErr(\"variable not found: Identifier(\\\"\" +String X +String \"\\\")\") requires notBool X in_keys(M)\n   166\t\n   167\t  syntax BoolResult ::= resolveBool(Operand, Map) [function, total]\n   168\t  rule resolveBool(O, M) => #toBool(resolve(O, M))\n   169\t  syntax BoolResult ::= #toBool(ValueResult) [function, total]\n   170\t  rule #toBool(vErr(S)) => boolErr(S)\n   171\t  rule #toBool(vOk(V)) => asBool(V)\n   172\t\n   173\t  syntax ValuesResult ::= vsOk(List) | vsErr(String)\n   174\t  syntax ValuesResult ::= resolveAll(Operands, Map) [function, total]\n   175\t  rule resolveAll(.Operands, _) => vsOk(.List)\n   176\t  rule resolveAll((O, Os), M) => #consValue(resolve(O, M), resolveAll(Os, M))\n   177\t  syntax ValuesResult ::= #consValue(ValueResult, ValuesResult) [function, total]\n   178\t  rule #consValue(vErr(S), _) => vsErr(S)\n   179\t  rule #consValue(vOk(_), vsErr(S)) => vsErr(S)\n   180\t  rule #consValue(vOk(V), vsOk(L)) => vsOk(ListItem(V) L)\n   181\t\n   182\t  // Write helpers: #put(name, result) stores or fails.\n   183\t  syntax KItem ::= #put(String, ValueResult) | #put2(String, String, PairResult) | #fail(String)\n   184\t  rule <k> #put(_, vErr(S)) => #fail(S) ... </k>\n   185\t  rule <k> #put(X, vOk(V)) => .K ... </k> <mem> M => M[X <- V] </mem>\n   186\t  rule <k> #put2(_, _, pErr(S)) => #fail(S) ... </k>\n   187\t  rule <k> #put2(X, Y, pOk(V, W)) => .K ... </k> <mem> M => M[X <- V][Y <- W] </mem>\n   188\t  rule <k> #fail(S) => .K ... </k> <status> ok() => error(S) </status>\n   189\t  syntax KItem ::= #check(CheckResult)\n   190\t  rule <k> #check(cOk()) => .K ... </k>\n   191\t  rule <k> #check(cErr(S)) => #fail(S) ... </k>\n   192\t\n   193\t  // --- Witness semantics, one rule per instruction (alive only) --------------------------\n   194\t  rule <k> #exec(add(A, B, O)) => #put(O, #bin(resolve(A, M), resolve(B, M), \"add\")) ... </k> <mem> M </mem> <status> ok() </status>\n   195\t  rule <k> #exec(mul(A, B, O)) => #put(O, #bin(resolve(A, M), resolve(B, M), \"mul\")) ... </k> <mem> M </mem> <status> ok() </status>\n   196\t  rule <k> #exec(testEq(A, B, O)) => #put(O, #bin(resolve(A, M), resolve(B, M), \"test_eq\")) ... </k> <mem> M </mem> <status> ok() </status>\n   197\t  rule <k> #exec(ecMul(A, S, O)) => #put(O, #bin(resolve(A, M), resolve(S, M), \"ec_mul\")) ... </k> <mem> M </mem> <status> ok() </status>\n   198\t  rule <k> #exec(fromCoordinates(X, Y, O)) => #put(O, #bin(resolve(X, M), resolve(Y, M), \"from_coordinates\")) ... </k> <mem> M </mem> <status> ok() </status>\n   199\t  rule <k> #exec(bytes32FromLowHigh(L, H, O)) => #put(O, #bin(resolve(L, M), resolve(H, M), \"bytes32_from_low_high\")) ... </k> <mem> M </mem> <status> ok() </status>\n   200\t  syntax ValueResult ::= #bin(ValueResult, ValueResult, String) [function, total]\n   201\t  rule #bin(vErr(S), _, _) => vErr(S)\n   202\t  rule #bin(vOk(_), vErr(S), _) => vErr(S)\n   203\t  rule #bin(vOk(A), vOk(B), \"add\") => addV(A, B)\n   204\t  rule #bin(vOk(A), vOk(B), \"mul\") => mulV(A, B)\n   205\t  rule #bin(vOk(A), vOk(B), \"test_eq\") => testEqV(A, B)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba experiments/zkir-k/tools/zkir_run.py | sed -n '235,335p'; nl -ba /home/charl/Moriarty/repos/input-output-hk/arc-zkir/docs/zkir-v3-spec.md | sed -n '585,625p;1156,1202p'; rg -n 'pub fn load|deny_unknown|PublicInput|guard:|version' /home/charl/Moriarty/repos/_extracts/ledger9-92e8bdd3-zkir-v3-src/zkir-v3/src/ir.rs | tail -30; ls /home/charl/Moriarty/repos/_build/midnight-zkir-2ffe2d1/zkir/src; nl -ba wiki/zkir/zkir-k-definition.md | tail -55; cat evidence/k-rust-compatibility-2026-09-05.txt\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba experiments/zkir-k/tools/zkir_run.py | sed -n '235,335p'; nl -ba /home/charl/Moriarty/repos/input-output-hk/arc-zkir/docs/zkir-v3-spec.md | sed -n '585,625p;1156,1202p'; rg -n 'pub fn load|deny_unknown|PublicInput|guard:|version' /home/charl/Moriarty/repos/_extracts/ledger9-92e8bdd3-zkir-v3-src/zkir-v3/src/ir.rs | tail -30; ls /home/charl/Moriarty/repos/_build/midnight-zkir-2ffe2d1/zkir/src; nl -ba wiki/zkir/zkir-k-definition.md | tail -55; cat evidence/k-rust-compatibility-2026-09-05.txt\"","aggregated_output":"   235\tSYMBOL_TO_TYPE.update({'Bool': 'Bool', 'Byte': 'Byte'})\n   236\t\n   237\t\n   238\tdef type_of_symbol(t: KInner) -> str:\n   239\t    assert isinstance(t, KApply)\n   240\t    if t.label.name == 'BytesN':\n   241\t        return f'Bytes<{tok_int(t.args[0])}>'\n   242\t    return SYMBOL_TO_TYPE[t.label.name]\n   243\t\n   244\t\n   245\tdef need(t: KInner) -> tuple[str, Any]:\n   246\t    assert isinstance(t, KApply)\n   247\t    match t.label.name:\n   248\t        case 'needPubOut':\n   249\t            return ('pubOut', type_of_symbol(t.args[0]))\n   250\t        case 'needPriv':\n   251\t            return ('priv', type_of_symbol(t.args[0]))\n   252\t        case 'needPubIn':\n   253\t            return ('pubIn', tok_int(t.args[0]))\n   254\t        case 'needComm':\n   255\t            return ('comm', tok_int(t.args[0]))\n   256\t    raise ValueError(t.label.name)\n   257\t\n   258\t\n   259\tdef skip(t: KInner):\n   260\t    assert isinstance(t, KApply)\n   261\t    if t.label.name == 'skipNone':\n   262\t        return None\n   263\t    return tok_int(t.args[0])\n   264\t\n   265\t\n   266\tclass Runner:\n   267\t    def __init__(self, definition: Path | None = None, ext: bool = False):\n   268\t        self.ext = ext\n   269\t        self.krun = KRun(definition or (default_ext_definition() if ext else default_definition()))\n   270\t\n   271\t    def run(self, program: KInner, preimage: dict[str, Any], depth: int | None = None, gen: bool = False) -> dict[str, Any]:\n   272\t        job = KApply('genJob' if gen else 'job', [program, preimage_term(preimage)])\n   273\t        kore = self.krun.kast_to_kore(job, KSort('Job'))\n   274\t        res = self.krun.run_process(kore, depth=depth)\n   275\t        if res.returncode != 0:\n   276\t            return {'status': 'krun-failed', 'error': res.stderr[-2000:]}\n   277\t        cfg = self.krun.kore_to_kast(KoreParser(res.stdout).pattern())\n   278\t        status = find_cell(cfg, '<status>')\n   279\t        assert isinstance(status, KApply)\n   280\t        out: dict[str, Any] = {}\n   281\t        if status.label.name == 'ok':\n   282\t            out['status'] = 'ok'\n   283\t        else:\n   284\t            out['status'] = 'error'\n   285\t            out['error'] = tok_str(status.args[0])\n   286\t        memory = {}\n   287\t        for k, v in map_items(find_cell(cfg, '<mem>')):\n   288\t            variant, enc = encode_value(v, self.ext)\n   289\t            memory[tok_str(k)] = {'variant': variant, 'encoded': [str(e) for e in enc]}\n   290\t        out['memory'] = memory\n   291\t        out['pis'] = [str(tok_int(x)) for x in list_items(find_cell(cfg, '<pi>'))]\n   292\t        out['pi_skips'] = [skip(x) for x in list_items(find_cell(cfg, '<skips>'))]\n   293\t        out['cursors'] = (tok_int(find_cell(cfg, '<pubInIdx>')), tok_int(find_cell(cfg, '<pubOutIdx>')), tok_int(find_cell(cfg, '<privIdx>')))\n   294\t        out['constraints'] = len(list_items(find_cell(cfg, '<constraints>')))\n   295\t        out['k_cell'] = self.krun.pretty_print(find_cell(cfg, '<k>')).strip()\n   296\t        out['needs'] = [need(x) for x in list_items(find_cell(cfg, '<needs>'))]\n   297\t        verdicts = list_items(find_cell(cfg, '<verdicts>'))\n   298\t        bad = []\n   299\t        for v in verdicts:\n   300\t            assert isinstance(v, KApply) and v.label.name == 'verdict'\n   301\t            outcome = v.args[1]\n   302\t            assert isinstance(outcome, KApply)\n   303\t            if outcome.label.name != 'holds':\n   304\t                gate = self.krun.pretty_print(v.args[0]).replace('\\n', ' ')\n   305\t                gate = ' '.join(gate.split())\n   306\t                bad.append((outcome.label.name, tok_str(outcome.args[0]) if outcome.args else '', gate[:120]))\n   307\t        out['verdicts'] = len(verdicts)\n   308\t        out['violations'] = bad\n   309\t        return out\n   310\t\n   311\t    def run_file(self, path: Path, preimage: dict[str, Any], gen: bool = False) -> dict[str, Any]:\n   312\t        return self.run(zkir_kast.load_program(path, ext=self.ext), preimage, gen=gen)\n   313\t\n   314\t\n   315\tdef main() -> int:\n   316\t    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n   317\t    ap.add_argument('file', type=Path)\n   318\t    ap.add_argument('preimage', type=Path)\n   319\t    ap.add_argument('--definition', type=Path, default=None)\n   320\t    ap.add_argument('--ext', action='store_true')\n   321\t    args = ap.parse_args()\n   322\t    runner = Runner(args.definition, ext=args.ext)\n   323\t    with open(args.preimage) as f:\n   324\t        pre = json.load(f)\n   325\t    print(json.dumps(runner.run_file(args.file, pre), indent=1))\n   326\t    return 0\n   327\t\n   328\t\n   329\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   330\t    sys.exit(main())\n   585\t  (`ir-source[v3-generic]` for the source, `ir-instruction[v3]` for\n   586\t  instructions, etc.) so the deserialiser refuses the wrong shape.\n   587\t\n   588\t### 5.3 Well-formedness\n   589\t\n   590\tAn `IrSource` is *well-formed* iff the following structural conditions hold.\n   591\tThey are necessary preconditions for §6 and §7; they are *not* sufficient for\n   592\tpreprocess success, which also depends on the preimage.\n   593\t\n   594\t- **WF1 — input arity / encoding.** The total encoded width of `inputs`,\n   595\t  `Σᵢ encoded_len(inputs[i].type)`, equals `|P.inputs|` at runtime (checked in\n   596\t  `preprocess`).\n   597\t- **WF2 — bit bounds.** Bit-count fields are bounded per-instruction:\n   598\t  - `ConstrainBits { bits }`, `LessThan { bits }`: `bits < FR_BITS`. Preprocess\n   599\t    rejects `bits ≥ FR_BITS` (\"Excessive bit bound\").\n   600\t  - `DivModPowerOfTwo { bits }`, `ReconstituteField { bits }`:\n   601\t    `bits ≤ FR_BYTES_STORED · 8` (`≤ 248`). Preprocess rejects beyond this.\n   602\t- **WF3 — arities.** `Encode` requires `|outputs| = encoded_len(type of input)`;\n   603\t  `DivModPowerOfTwo` requires exactly 2 outputs; `Output` requires\n   604\t  `|vals| = |IrSource.outputs|`.  (`PersistentHash` / `Keccak256` bind a\n   605\t  single `Bytes32` output, so they carry no arity side-condition.)\n   606\t  (The pair-typed `IntoCoordinates`, `FromCoordinates`, `Bytes32IntoLowHigh`,\n   607\t  `Bytes32FromLowHigh` fix their arity structurally.)\n   608\t- **WF4 — define-before-use.** Every `Variable` operand names a register bound\n   609\t  by an earlier instruction (or a declared input). Re-binding an existing name\n   610\t  is checked for consistency at synthesis (`mem_insert` in `ir_vm.rs`) —\n   611\t  except by `FromBytes32`, `ReverseBytes`, `Bytes32IntoLowHigh`, and\n   612\t  `Bytes32FromLowHigh`, which bypass `mem_insert` with a raw\n   613\t  `memory.insert` — so the prover-side check does not cover those bindings;\n   614\t  the intended discipline is single assignment.\n   615\t- **WF5 — `Impact` discipline.** Each `Impact` declares its own group of\n   616\t  `|inputs|` public inputs and its own guard, so public-input coverage is\n   617\t  structural rather than a separate obligation (§6.4, §7.2).\n   618\t\n   619\tOperand type-compatibility (e.g. `Add` on two `Native`s) is **not** a\n   620\twell-formedness condition in this sense — it is enforced dynamically and is the\n   621\tcontent of the support matrix (Appendix B). A type mismatch is a runtime error\n   622\tof both preprocess and synthesis.\n   623\t\n   624\t---\n   625\t\n  1156\t### 8.2 Producer obligations\n  1157\t\n  1158\tThe converse of completeness fails for arbitrary sources. Section 7.0 lists the\n  1159\tpreconditions the chips assume rather than enforce, and §7.2 the points where\n  1160\tthe circuit is laxer than preprocess; a source that does not close those gaps\n  1161\tdenotes a constraint system with satisfying witnesses that correspond to no\n  1162\trun. The obligations below close them. They are the responsibility of the\n  1163\tproducer of the IR — in practice the Compact compiler — and all are decidable:\n  1164\tthe mechanisation supplies a runnable checker for each.\n  1165\t\n  1166\t**O1 — Single assignment.** Every identifier an instruction binds is fresh: no\n  1167\tinstruction rebinds a name already bound by an earlier instruction or declared\n  1168\tas an input, and the declared input names are pairwise distinct. Rebinding is\n  1169\tnot a circuit constraint (§7.1), and four instructions bypass even the\n  1170\tprover-side consistency check (WF4, §5.3); the commitment moreover re-encodes\n  1171\tthe *final* value of each input name (§7.4). Checker: `producer-SA?`.\n  1172\t\n  1173\t**O2 — Value typing.** Every operand is bound with the type its instruction\n  1174\texpects, per Appendix B, and no `ConstrainEq`/`TestEq` operand is a\n  1175\t`JubjubScalar`. A source violating this errors at both preprocess and\n  1176\tsynthesis; the obligation makes the type of every cell a static property of the\n  1177\tsource, which is what lets a satisfying witness be read back as a run. Being a\n  1178\tstatement about a chain of typing contexts, it presupposes O1 and so subsumes\n  1179\tit. Checker: `producer-WT?`.\n  1180\t\n  1181\t**O3 — Bit bounds.** The WF2 bounds of §5.3 (`bits < FR_BITS` for\n  1182\t`ConstrainBits`/`LessThan`, `bits ≤ 248` for\n  1183\t`DivModPowerOfTwo`/`ReconstituteField`). Preprocess rejects violations\n  1184\tdynamically, but the circuit does not: for an out-of-range `bits` the emitted\n  1185\trange constraints remain satisfiable, so the bound has to hold of the *source*\n  1186\tfor a satisfying witness to be extractable as a run of the reference\n  1187\timplementation. Checker: `producer-WF2?`.\n  1188\t\n  1189\t**O4 — Witness shape.** Unlike O1–O3 this is a condition on a witness, not on a\n  1190\tsource: it collects the §6.6(d) premises the lowering leaves unenforced, and\n  1191\tthe extraction results of §8.4 are stated for witnesses satisfying it. It\n  1192\trequires that the cells filled by transcript reads inhabit their declared type\n  1193\tand round-trip through the encoding of §4, that read guards are boolean, that\n  1194\teach `Assert` operand is exactly `1` (the circuit only forces `≠ 0`, §7.2),\n  1195\tthat each `ReconstituteField` result does not overflow `Fr`, that `LessThan`\n  1196\toperands meet the exact `2^bits` bound rather than the evened bound the chip\n  1197\tenforces (§7.2), and that each `DivModPowerOfTwo` binds two outputs. The\n  1198\tcondition is not restrictive for honest provers — every canonical witness\n  1199\tsatisfies it (§8.4) — so it excludes only witnesses exploiting the slack the\n  1200\tcircuit genuinely leaves. Checker: `WShape?`.\n  1201\t\n  1202\t### 8.3 P5 — Preprocess–circuit faithfulness\n38:    /// The minor version of this IR.\n39:    pub version: IrMinorVersion,\n64:#[tag = \"ir-minor-version[v3]\"]\n485:        guard: Operand,\n877:    PublicInput {\n880:        guard: Option<Operand>,\n897:    /// NB: This instruction is essentially identical to `PublicInput` except that\n903:        guard: Option<Operand>,\n955:    pub fn load<R: Read>(reader: R) -> io::Result<Self> {\n960:                    obj.get(\"version\")\n963:                            \"Expected a version entry\",\n973:                            \"version\".into(),\n980:                        format!(\"Unhandled version: {major}.{minor}\"),\nir.rs\nir_instructions\nir_types.rs\nir_vm.rs\nlib.rs\nmain.rs\n    15\tThis page records what the executable K definition of ZKIR v3 under `experiments/zkir-k/` is, how it was checked, and what the checks found. The decisions it implements are on [../zkir-k-semantics-plan.md](../zkir-k-semantics-plan.md); the instruction set, types and VM it formalises are described on [zkir-instruction-set.md](zkir-instruction-set.md), [zkir-type-system.md](zkir-type-system.md) and [zkir-vm-semantics.md](zkir-vm-semantics.md). Everything here was reproduced on 2026-09-05 with K v7.1.337 and the receipts named in each claim.\n    16\t\n    17\t## Layout\n    18\t\n    19\tThe definition is one K definition split into modules, each with the Rust file it follows in its header (CLM-0731; experiments/zkir-k/semantics; repository observation; reproduced; high; S1):\n    20\t\n    21\t| Module | File | Follows | Content |\n    22\t|---|---|---|---|\n    23\t| `ZKIR-SYNTAX`, `ZKIR-WF` | `zkir-syntax.k` | `ir.rs`, `ir_types.rs` | 34 instructions, 13 types, operands, guards, alignments; `reads`, `writes`, `encodedLen`; static well-formedness |\n    24\t| `ZKIR-FIELD` | `zkir-field.k` | `transient-crypto/src/curve.rs`, midnight-curves 0.3.1 | eight moduli, modular arithmetic on K `Int`, Tonelli-Shanks square roots |\n    25\t| `ZKIR-CURVES` | `zkir-curves.k` | midnight-curves 0.3.1, midnight-circuits 7.2.4 `ecc/curves.rs` | affine twisted-Edwards (Jubjub, Curve25519) and Weierstrass (secp256k1, secp256r1) arithmetic, subgroup tests, Jubjub decompression |\n    26\t| `ZKIR-VALUES` | `zkir-values.k` | `ir_instructions/encode.rs`, midnight-circuits `Instantiable` | the 13 value constructors, `encode_offcircuit`, `from_public_input`, input decoding |\n    27\t| `ZKIR-CONSTANTS` | `zkir-constants.k` (generated) | midnight-circuits `hash/poseidon/constants/blstrs.rs`, `ecc/hash_to_curve/mtc_params.rs` | 204 Poseidon round constants, the MDS matrix, the Shallue-van de Woestijne parameters |\n    28\t| `ZKIR-HASH` | `zkir-hash.k` | midnight-circuits `poseidon_cpu.rs`, `htc_gadget.rs`, `mtc_cpu.rs`; FIPS 180-4; Keccak | Poseidon sponge (fixed and variable length), hash-to-curve, SHA-256, Keccak-256 |\n    29\t| `ZKIR-OPS` | `zkir-ops.k` | `ir_instructions/*.rs` off-circuit halves, `transient-crypto/src/{fab,repr}.rs` | one function per `*_offcircuit`, boolean and bit-bound resolution, aligned byte layout for the standard hashes |\n    30\t| `ZKIR-VM` | `zkir-vm.k` | `ir_vm.rs` `preprocess` | the configuration, sequencing, one witness rule per instruction, constraint emission, transcript and commitment checks, generation mode |\n    31\t| `ZKIR-CONSTRAINTS` | `zkir-constraints.k` | `ir_vm.rs` `circuit`, `ir_instructions/*.rs` in-circuit halves, `used_chips` | the in-circuit relation of each gate, evaluated on the final witness |\n    32\t| `ZKIR-EXT` | `zkir-ext.k`, `zkir-sha512-constants.k` | `midnight-zkir` 2ffe2d1 `zkir/src/` | Bool, Byte, Bytes<n>; and, or, xor, concat, slice, nth, reverse, load_constant, sha512 |\n    33\t\n    34\tPrograms enter through `tools/zkir_kast.py`, which reads the JSON artifact and builds the `Program` term with pyk, mirroring the serde layer of `ir.rs` (variables start with `%`, immediates are little-endian hex below r, `guard: null`, tagged alignments); the same script rejects what `IrSource::load` rejects (CLM-0732; experiments/zkir-k/tools/zkir_kast.py; repository observation; reproduced; high; S1). A run is `job(Program, Preimage)`, where the preimage mirrors `ProofPreimage`: raw inputs, binding input, optional commitment and opening, private transcript, public transcript inputs and outputs (CLM-0732).\n    35\t\n    36\t## What a run produces\n    37\t\n    38\tThe configuration carries the seven components of the VM page as cells (`<mem>`, `<pi>`, `<skips>`, `<pubInIdx>`, `<pubOutIdx>`, `<privIdx>`, `<outputs>`) plus `<constraints>`, `<status>`, `<chips>` and `<verdicts>` (CLM-0733; experiments/zkir-k/semantics/zkir-vm.k; repository observation; reproduced; high; S1). Each instruction first appends its gate to `<constraints>` and then runs its witness half; the first witness error sets `<status>` and freezes the witness cells while every later instruction still emits its gate, so the constraint set at the end is always the whole circuit's (CLM-0733). At the end, the transcripts must be fully consumed and, when the program declares a communications commitment, the commitment must equal the Poseidon commitment of the raw inputs and the encoded outputs, exactly as in `preprocess` (CLM-0733). Finally every gate is evaluated against the witness and `<verdicts>` records, per gate, whether it holds, is violated, cannot be synthesised (a missing in-circuit dispatch arm or an uninitialised chip), or is unknown because the witness stopped before the register existed (CLM-0733).\n    39\t\n    40\tGates are instruction-level relations, not PLONKish gate rows. `gate(add(a, b, o))` states that register `o` equals the sum of `a` and `b` under the type dispatch of `add_incircuit`; `gate(assert(c))` states `c` is non-zero; `piGate(i, g, x)` states that public input `i` equals `x` when the boolean `g` is 1 and 0 otherwise (CLM-0734; experiments/zkir-k/semantics/zkir-constraints.k; repository observation; reproduced; high; S1). Because the relation is evaluated on the concrete witness, a run establishes that the honest witness satisfies the emitted constraints, never that no other witness does; soundness stays with the arc-zkir theorems, as the plan says (CLM-0734).\n    41\t\n    42\t## How it was checked\n    43\t\n    44\tThree layers, each with its receipt:\n    45\t\n    46\t1. Unit checks against an independent Python implementation of the same formulas (`tools/unit_values.py`): field inverses and square roots, the non-residuosity of both Edwards `d` constants, the Jubjub subgroup generator as eight times the curve generator, scalar multiples on all four curves, the order of each generator, encode and decode round trips for every type, and the parity-only behaviour of Jubjub decompression. 41 of 41 pass (CLM-0726).\n    47\t2. Known-answer checks against the Rust crate for the hashes (`tools/unit_hash.py`): Poseidon on zero to three inputs, hash-to-curve on zero to three inputs, SHA-256 and Keccak-256 through one-, 32- and 232-byte aligned preimages, and the aligned byte layout itself. 18 of 18 pass; Poseidon and hash-to-curve matched on the first run, which also confirms that the crate's paired partial rounds are an algebraic rewrite of the plain round function (CLM-0726).\n    48\t3. Differential runs against the crate's own `preprocess` (`tools/diff_test.py`). The harness draws typed raw inputs, runs the K definition in generation mode until the transcript needs are stable, then runs K and `zkir-oracle` on the same preimage and compares status, every register's variant and encoding, the public-input vector and the skip vector. Over the 65 programs of the corpus, 314 comparisons agree and none disagree; 37 are successful witness runs, the rest compare error paths (CLM-0728). All gates hold on every successful run (CLM-0729).\n    49\t\n    50\tThe corpus is the 43 inline programs of the crate's tests at 92e8bdd3 (seeded with their literal inputs where the tests give them), the six version-3 micro-dao precompiles of midnight-zkir 2ffe2d1, the seven Moriarty escrow and swap artifacts, nine handmade programs that exercise every instruction on every type it supports, and seven handmade negatives for the static checks (CLM-0724, CLM-0728). The escrow, swap and micro-dao programs never reach a successful witness with generated inputs, because their assertions need a consistent transaction context; for them the harness compares error paths only (CLM-0728).\n    51\t\n    52\t## What the checks found\n    53\t\n    54\t- The thirteen findings of the arc-zkir divergence review reproduce as programs (`tools/divergence_tests.py`): for each, the off-circuit status agrees between K and the crate, and the gate outcome is the one the review describes, for example `assert` of 2 fails off-circuit while its gate holds, `cond_select` on Bytes32 and `constrain_eq` on JubjubScalar succeed off-circuit while their gates are synthesis errors, `bytes32_from_low_high` with a foreign `high` succeeds off-circuit while its gate is a synthesis error, `less_than` with a 3-bit bound rejects 8 off-circuit while the padded 4-bit gate would accept it, a program touching secp256k1 only through `from_bytes32` succeeds off-circuit while its gate reports the chip uninitialised, and the order-2 Curve25519 point is rejected on both sides (CLM-0730).\n    55\t- One divergence not in the review: Jubjub `from_coordinates` off-circuit goes through point decompression and uses only the parity of `x`, so `(x+2, y)` yields the true point on both K and the crate while the exact-coordinate gate is violated; the Agda trust base assumes the exact behaviour (CLM-0735; evidence/zkir-k-divergence-tests-2026-09-05.txt case `k01` and repos/input-output-hk/arc-zkir/src/zkir-v3/Assumptions.agda `fromCoordsJ-coordsJ`; executed test; reproduced; high; S1). Recorded in [../contradictions.md](../contradictions.md).\n    56\t- The Rust `preprocess` does not enforce single assignment; the K static check does, so a program that rewrites a register is rejected by K before the run and accepted by the crate (CLM-0725). No program in the corpus does this.\n    57\t- Error messages agree in substance; the only textual difference is the crate printing field elements as little-endian hex where K prints decimals (CLM-0728).\n    58\t\n    59\t## The extension surface\n    60\t\n    61\t`ZKIR-EXT` is a second main module on the same definition for the standalone `midnight-zkir` crate at 2ffe2d1: the types Bool, Byte and Bytes<n> (Bytes<32> keeps the base representation so every base rule applies), the instructions `and`, `or`, `xor` over Bool, `concat`, `slice`, `nth`, `reverse` over byte strings, `load_constant` from a typed raw encoding, `sha512`, logical `neg` on Bool, and the canonical-form check that 2ffe2d1's decoder performs by re-encoding every decoded value; `reverse_bytes` is rejected at the preprocessor as the crate removed it (CLM-0739; experiments/zkir-k/semantics/zkir-ext.k; repository observation; reproduced; high; S1). Against a second `zkir-oracle` built from that crate, 61 of its inline test programs, the six micro-dao precompiles and the handmade programs give 366 comparisons that all agree, with 40 successful runs and no non-holding gate (CLM-0737). The canonical-form check is the visible behavioural difference between the two crates: a Jubjub point input with a wrong `x` of the right parity is accepted at 92e8bdd3 and rejected at 2ffe2d1 (CLM-0737).\n    62\t\n    63\tA second new finding came out of this run (K2): both crates slice the transcript directly, so an unguarded `public_input` or `private_input` whose transcript is too short panics with an index-out-of-range rather than returning an error; K reports an error, and the divergence test `k02` reproduces the panic through the oracle (CLM-0738).\n    64\t\n    65\t## The other oracles\n    66\t\n    67\tThe arc-zkir v3 Agda development type-checks in full with its own Nix toolchain, fifteen modules under `--safe` (CLM-0736; evidence/arc-zkir-agda-typecheck-2026-09-05.txt; executed test; reproduced; high; S1). It cannot execute programs: it is parametric over an `Assumptions` record that supplies the field, curve and hash primitives, and the repository has no concrete instance of that record, so oracle 3 of the plan remains a correspondence by reading, not by running (CLM-0736; repos/input-output-hk/arc-zkir/src/zkir-v3/Assumptions.agda; repository observation; reproduced; high; S4).\n    68\t\n    69\tMidnight's `k-rust` (0.4.0, built from the pinned checkout) runs the K tutorial lesson in three seconds and parses terms of `ZKIR-SYNTAX` in under four, but neither `krust krun` on a one-instruction program nor `krust kcompile` of the full definition finished: the compile was killed after 25 minutes of CPU with no output, where canonical K compiles the same definition in twenty seconds (CLM-0740; evidence/k-rust-compatibility-2026-09-05.txt; executed test; reproduced; high; S1). The definition uses nothing k-rust documents as unsupported, so the gap is performance of its frontend pipeline on a definition of this size, not a feature boundary; running the semantics inside the Midnight TypeScript tooling stays a goal, as the plan said, not a gate (CLM-0740).\n# k-rust compatibility attempt, 2026-09-05\n\nk-rust 0.4.0 built from repos/midnightntwrk/k-rust (687ccd0) with cargo build --release -p k-rust (4m35s).\n\n1. krust krun toolchain-check/lesson-02-a.k --main-module LESSON-02-A --sort Color -e 'colorOf(Banana())': exit 0 in 2.9 s, result Yellow.\n2. krust kast semantics/zkir-syntax.k --module ZKIR-SYNTAX --sort IrType --expression 'native()': exit 0 in 3.5 s, result `Native`(.KList).\n3. krust krun semantics/zkir.k --main-module ZKIR --sort Job -e '<job term of test_minimal_proof>': no result within the 10-minute tool limit; killed.\n4. timeout 1500 krust kcompile semantics/zkir.k --main-module ZKIR --syntax-module ZKIR-VM-SYNTAX: exit 124 (timed out after 25 minutes, 17+ minutes CPU, ~105 MB RSS, no output, no KORE emitted).\n\nVerdict: the k-rust frontend accepts the definition's syntax but does not finish compiling the full definition in 25 minutes; canonical K compiles it in 20 s.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
